/* 段落记忆 · 词层 1 · 子块 b：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(1,{"sub":"b","par":{"hide":{"tw":[["cover",3],["change",2],["skin",0],["conceal",0],["find",6],["harbor",3],["earth",3],["reveal",6]],"en":"The little fox knows how to hide. It will cover its body with dry leaves and change the colour of its coat with the seasons. In the cold months its skin turns white, which is the best way to conceal itself on snow. We could not find it for a whole week. One morning, near the harbor, it sat on the black earth beside a boat and looked at us. It had been sleeping under that same boat the whole time. Then it moved, and the light seemed to reveal a thin line of red fur along its back.","zh":"那只小狐狸很会藏。它用干叶子盖住身子，还随季节变换毛色。天冷的那几个月，它的皮毛转成白色，这是雪地里最好的隐藏办法。整整一周我们都没找到它。有天早上，在港口附近，它坐在一条船边的黑土上看着我们。接着它一动，光似乎把背脊上一道细细的红毛露了出来。"},"join":{"tw":[["unite",0],["connect",2],["junction",4],["joiner",4],["fair",3],["close",3],["union",0],["meet",6]],"en":"Two villages decided to join their small schools. The teachers wanted to unite the classes and connect the old halls with a new path. At the junction of the two roads the workers built a wide gate, and a joiner made the wooden doors by hand. The two head teachers meet every Monday to plan the week. On the day of the fair, families from both sides came close to the stage and watched the children sing. The union of two schools was not easy, but now nobody can tell which child came from which side.","zh":"两个村子决定把各自的小学合并。老师们想把班级并在一起，用一条新路把两座旧校舍连起来。在两条路的交叉口，工人们修了一座宽门，一位木匠手工做了那两扇木门。两位校长每周一碰头商量这一周的安排。集市那天，两边的家庭都凑到台前看孩子们唱歌。两校合一并不容易，但现在没人分得清哪个孩子来自哪一边。"},"judge":{"tw":[["judicial",4],["judiciary",4],["adjudicate",4],["guess",0],["decide",2],["try",0],["court",6],["jury",6],["think",2]],"en":"Nobody wanted to judge that case. The judicial system moves slowly here, and the judiciary in our town has only two small rooms. First the jury has to listen to both sides, then the judge has to decide. You cannot guess; you have to try every door and think about what is fair. To adjudicate a case like this takes weeks. Two old men sat at the back of the court all day and said nothing. When the decision finally came, the judge wrote three long pages, and everybody went home tired.","zh":"没人愿意审那个案子。这里的司法体系走得很慢，我们镇上的司法部门只有两间小屋。首先要由陪审团听双方陈述，然后由法官作出裁决。你不能靠猜，必须试遍每一条门路，想清楚什么是公平的。裁决这样一个案子要好几周。两个老人整天坐在法庭后排，一言不发。裁决终于下来时，法官写了三页长文，所有人都疲惫地回了家。"},"enter":{"tw":[["entrance",4],["entry",4],["board",3],["exit",1],["record",0],["book",3],["figure",0],["leave",6]],"en":"You cannot enter the old hall through the front entrance any more. The entry in the book says the door was closed in 1974. If you want to go in, board the small bus at the gate and get off at the north exit; the guard will record your name in a thin notebook. I do not know the exact figure of visitors each year, but we never leave the place before six. The key is kept in a shop across the street, and the woman there will only give it to people she already knows.","zh":"你不能再从正门进入那座旧礼堂了。簿子上的记录说那扇门 1974 年就封了。想进去的话，在大门口坐上小巴，从北门下车，守卫会把你的名字记在一个薄本子里。我不知道每年访客的确切数字，但我们从不早于六点离开。钥匙存在街对面的一家店里，那位女士只把钥匙交给她认识的人。"},"form":{"tw":[["formation",4],["formative",4],["build",0],["class",0],["course",0],["body",2],["change",2]],"en":"The formation of a good habit takes months. My formative years were spent in a small school where the class was tiny and the course was fixed for the whole year. We had to build a routine and keep the body moving every morning before the bell. One small change in the order of things, and the whole form of the day falls apart. One winter our teacher was ill for a week, and everything we had built came apart in three days. The next year we were told to build it again, and the form we found was not quite the same.","zh":"养成一个好习惯要花几个月。我的成长岁月是在一所小学校度过的，那里班级很小，课程整年都固定不变。我们得建立起一套作息，每天早晨铃响前让身体活动起来。只要顺序上有一点小改动，一整天的形态就散了。有一年冬天老师病了一周，我们建起来的那套东西三天就垮了。第二年他们让我们重新建起来，而重新找到的那个形态已经不太一样了。"},"head":{"tw":[["heady",4],["header",4],["lead",0],["mind",0],["control",2],["chair",3],["foot",1],["chief",6]],"en":"After two cups of that strong wine I felt heady and could hardly stand. My head was hot and my mind was not clear at all. Our chief engineer took control of the meeting, and the chair of the board sat at the end of the long table and did not lead the talk at all. A small header on the first page said 'Do not open'. From head to foot I felt the same strange heat, but nobody at the table seemed to notice; they drank water and went on working.","zh":"喝了两杯那种烈酒之后我觉得头晕，几乎站不住。我的头很热，脑子一点也不清楚。我们的总工程师掌控了会议，而董事会主席坐在长桌尽头，完全没有主导讨论。第一页上有一行小标题写着「请勿打开」。从头到脚我都感到同样奇怪的热，可桌上似乎没人察觉，他们喝着水继续干活。"},"heart":{"tw":[["hearty",4],["cardiac",4],["centre",0],["middle",0],["seat",3],["pain",6],["eye",0],["brain",6]],"en":"My grandfather had a cardiac problem last year. The doctor put a small machine in the centre of his chest, right in the middle, next to the heart. He still gets a pain in the left arm sometimes, but he eats a hearty breakfast and laughs a lot. His brain and his eye are fine, he says; it is only the seat of the trouble that is old. Every afternoon he walks to the end of the street and back, and the machine in his chest keeps the time for him.","zh":"我祖父去年心脏出了毛病。医生在他胸口正中央、紧贴心脏的位置放了一个小装置。他左臂有时还会痛，但他早餐吃得很香，也常笑。他说自己的脑子和眼睛都没问题，年久失修的只是毛病所在的那一处。每天下午他都走到街尾再折回来，胸里那个装置替他计着时间。"},"heat":{"tw":[["geothermal",4],["thermal",4],["cool",1],["cold",6],["temperature",6],["fry",3],["soak",3],["passion",0]],"en":"The geothermal water under this town is very hot. In winter we use it for the thermal baths, and the temperature stays near forty degrees all year. I like to soak in it for an hour, then run outside into the cold air to cool down. My friend cooks an egg in the steam and tries to fry bread on a flat stone. He has a passion for that sort of thing, and the heat never bothers him. In summer the same pipes carry cold water to every house on the street.","zh":"这个小镇地下的地热水很烫。冬天我们用地热浴室，水温全年保持在四十度左右。我喜欢在里面泡上一个小时，再跑到外面的冷空气里降温。我朋友在蒸汽里煮鸡蛋，还试着在一块平石上煎面包。他对这类事情极有热情，再热也从不介意。到了夏天，同一批管子给街上每户人家送冷水。"},"lay":{"tw":[["layer",4],["position",0],["pose",0],["load",3],["organize",2],["bare",6],["move",2],["hand",6]],"en":"We had to lay the old floor again. First we took off the top layer and put every board in the same position on the grass. The workers organize the load into two piles, and I help to hand them the nails. Do not move the wet ones, they say, they will crack in the sun. When the floor is bare, my sister likes to pose for a photograph there. I lay my hand on the cold stone underneath and rest, because the stone is older than the house itself.","zh":"我们得把旧地板重新铺一遍。先揭掉最上面一层，把每块木板按原样摆在草地上。工人们把货分成两堆，我帮忙递钉子。他们说湿的那些别动，太阳一晒会裂。地板露出来以后，我妹妹喜欢在那儿摆姿势拍照。我把手放在底下冰冷的石头上歇一会儿，因为那石头比房子本身还老。"},"line":{"tw":[["lining",4],["liner",4],["air",0],["blood",0],["business",0],["cover",2],["fill",2],["face",3]],"en":"There is a long line at the door of the shop every morning. The lining of my coat is torn, so I wear the old wool liner under it. People in the line talk about the air, about their blood pressure, about business. When the shop opens we fill the small room and cover the counter with our bags. I never see the same face twice. By nine the bread is always gone and the line simply disappears, as if it had never been there. I stand in it anyway, every morning, because the wait is the only part of my day that belongs to me.","zh":"每天早上那家店门口都排着长队。我外套的衬里破了，所以里面套着一件旧羊毛内衬。排队的人聊空气、聊血压、聊生意。店门一开，我们就挤满那间小屋，把包堆在柜台上。我从来没见过重复的脸。到九点面包必定卖完，队伍就那样消失了，仿佛从没出现过。但我每天早上还是去排，因为等待是我一天里唯一属于我自己的那段时间。"},"home":{"tw":[["homely",4],["homestead",3],["house",2],["family",0],["return",2],["away",1],["lodge",3],["rest",6],["environment",2]],"en":"My idea of home is a homely room with one window. The house is small, but the homestead behind it has been in our family for four generations. When I return from the city I sleep for twelve hours; away from it I cannot rest at all. My friends lodge in a hotel two streets from here and say the environment is the same anywhere. I tell them they are wrong, and that one room you know is worth more than a big one you do not. They return to the city on Sunday, and I stay here another week.","zh":"我心目中的家是一个带一扇窗的朴素房间。房子很小，可屋后那片宅地已属于我们家四代人了。从城里回来时我能睡上十二个小时；离开它我就完全无法休息。我的朋友们住在两条街外的一家旅馆，说环境在哪里都一样。我告诉他们他们错了，一间你熟悉的屋子比一间你不熟悉的大屋子值钱得多。他们周日回城里去，我在这儿再待一周。"},"let":{"tw":[["letter",4],["allow",3],["accept",2],["prevent",1],["rent",0],["lease",0],["admit",3],["leave",2]],"en":"They will not let us sign the lease before June. The letter says the owner will allow three people in the flat, but he will not accept a dog. Nothing can prevent him from changing his mind either, and he will not admit that the price is too high. We rent the top floor now and pay by the week. If he decides to leave the country, we will have to find another place before the summer ends. The dog sleeps under the table in the kitchen and has never once barked at anybody.","zh":"他们不允许我们在六月前签租约。信上说房东允许三个人住这套公寓，但不接受养狗。也没什么能阻止他改主意，而他也不肯承认价格太高。我们现在租顶层，按周付钱。如果他决定出国，我们就得在夏天结束前另找住处。"},"light":{"tw":[["lightly",4],["clean",0],["clear",0],["flood",3],["surface",6],["dark",1],["burn",2],["match",3],["easy",5]],"en":"The light in this room is strange. It is clean and clear in the morning, when a flood of sun hits the white surface of the wall, but by four o'clock it is almost dark. I burn one candle and read by it, or I strike a match and walk to the window. Sleep comes lightly here; the dark does not feel heavy and the light does not hurt my eyes. It is easy to work in this room, and just as easy to stop working. When the sun goes I light the lamp, and the room looks clear again.","zh":"这屋子里的光很奇怪。清晨它干净而清澈，一大片阳光打在墙的白色表面上，可到四点就几乎黑了。我点一支蜡烛就着光读书，或者划根火柴走到窗前。在这里睡觉很浅；黑暗并不沉重，光也不刺眼。在这屋里很容易干活，也同样很容易就停下不干。太阳一落我就点灯，屋子看上去又变得清晰起来。"},"face":{"tw":[["facial",4],["front",2],["bottom",3],["cover",2],["look",0],["top",3],["lie",2],["present",0]],"en":"I did not want to face him again. His face was in the front room, at the top of the stairs, and the look on it had not changed at all. He would not lie down and sat in the chair by the window all night. The bottom of the door was covered with old letters that nobody had opened. His facial expression was calm, too calm. At present I still do not know what I said to him that evening. The front door was open, and his coat was on the top step where he left it.","zh":"我不想再面对他。他的脸在前面那间屋里、楼梯顶端，脸上的表情一点没变。他不肯躺下，整夜坐在窗边那把椅子上。门的下半部堆满了没人拆过的旧信。他的面部表情很平静，平静得过分。直到现在我也不知道那天晚上我对他说了什么。前门开着，他的外套还留在他放的那个最高一级台阶上。"},"fire":{"tw":[["fiery",4],["burn",0],["bake",2],["hire",1],["raise",0],["excite",3],["explosion",6],["attack",2]],"en":"The fire started in the bakery at two. The old oven was still burning when we came, and the smell of baked bread was everywhere in the street. Someone raised the alarm, and the explosion of the gas bottle woke the whole neighbourhood. It was a fiery hour, and the thought of it still excites me. Nobody knows what could attack the wiring like that. They will not hire a new baker until the roof is fixed. The cat was found two streets away the next morning, asleep under a car.","zh":"火灾是两点在面包房起的。我们赶到时那个旧烤炉还在烧，街上到处是烤面包的味道。有人拉响了警报，煤气瓶的爆炸惊醒了整个街区。那是火光冲天的一小时，现在想起来还让我激动。没人知道是什么能那样侵蚀线路。屋顶修好之前他们不会雇新面包师。"},"fix":{"tw":[["fixture",4],["cook",0],["care",3],["better",2],["plug",6],["doctor",0],["dress",3],["hole",0]],"en":"Can you fix this lamp? The fixture is loose and the plug is broken. My brother cooked dinner while I worked, and my sister dressed the children and put them to bed. There is a hole in the wall behind the lamp that I cannot fill. The doctor who lived here before us took better care of this house than we ever did. I will fix it properly on Sunday. Until then we will sit in the dark and talk, which is not such a bad thing. The children do not mind the dark at all, and my brother cooks better by candlelight.","zh":"你能修一下这盏灯吗？灯具松了，插头也坏了。我干活时我哥哥做了晚饭，我姐姐给孩子们穿好衣服哄他们上床。灯后面墙上有个洞，我填不上。住在我们之前的那位医生对这房子比我们上心得多。我周日会好好修它。在那之前我们就摸黑坐着说话，这也算不上什么坏事。孩子们一点也不介意黑，我哥哥在烛光下做得反而更好。"},"green":{"tw":[["greenery",4],["park",0],["sprout",3],["site",2],["ripe",1],["emerald",3],["vegetable",2]],"en":"The green field behind the house turns yellow in July. The greenery along the river is thick, and in spring every small sprout comes up between the stones. We chose the site for the new park because it stays green all year. The emerald water below the bridge is cold, and the vegetable garden next to it is not ripe yet. My mother says green is the only colour she can trust. She has planted the same three rows for forty years. In winter the field is grey, but the sprout in the window stays green all year.","zh":"屋后那片绿色的田到七月就变黄了。河边的草木很茂密，春天每一个小芽都从石缝里钻出来。我们把新公园选在这里，是因为它整年都是绿的。桥下那水呈翡翠色，很凉；旁边的菜园还没熟。我母亲说绿色是她唯一能信任的颜色。同一片三行地她种了四十年。冬天田野是灰的，可窗台上那株小苗整年都是绿的。"},"hand":{"tw":[["manual",4],["deal",3],["pass",0],["reach",0],["left",3],["right",3],["side",2],["hard",6]],"en":"Take my hand and do not let go. The manual says you must deal with the switch with your left hand only, and pass nothing to the other side of the machine. If you can reach the lever, pull it once and pull it hard. On the right there is a small wheel, and on the back a box of tools. My grandfather worked with either hand and never read a manual in his life. He says the hand knows more than the head, and for this job he is right.","zh":"抓住我的手，别松开。手册上说，操作这个开关只能用左手，而且不能把任何东西递到机器的另一侧。如果你够得到那根杠杆，就拉一次，用力拉。右边有个小轮子，后面有个工具箱。我祖父两只手都能干活，一辈子没读过手册。他说手比脑子懂得多，干这活儿他说得对。"},"lock":{"tw":[["locker",4],["curl",0],["engage",0],["hold",2],["hook",6],["mesh",0],["hair",2],["prop",6]],"en":"The lock on the old locker is broken. Inside there is a rope, a metal hook and a piece of mesh that used to hold the window shut. You have to engage the small lever first, then turn the key twice, and only then will the prop stay in place. My sister's hair was caught in it once, in a single curl, and she has never touched the door since. I keep a spare key in my pocket for the days when it refuses to open. The locker is empty now, and the hook still holds the mesh in place.","zh":"那个旧储物柜的锁坏了。里面有一根绳子、一个金属钩子，还有一块以前用来顶住窗户的铁丝网。你得先把小杠杆卡上，然后把钥匙转两圈，这样撑杆才待得住。我姐姐的头发曾被卷进去过一缕，从那以后她再没碰过那扇门。我在口袋里放了一把备用钥匙，专对付它打不开的日子。柜子现在是空的，钩子还挂着那块铁丝网。"},"father":{"tw":[["paternal",4],["mother",1],["patriarch",3],["head",2],["grandfather",6],["generate",0],["parent",2],["engender",0]],"en":"My father was born in a house that no longer exists. His paternal grandfather, an old patriarch, was the head of a family of eleven. My mother says the two of them could generate an argument out of nothing, and that noise would engender more noise. Every parent in that street knew everybody else's business. My father never spoke of it, and I only learned the whole story from my aunt. My mother kept a photograph of the old house in a drawer for forty years, and then it was lost.","zh":"我父亲出生在一栋如今已不存在的房子里。他父系那边的祖父，一位老家长，是十一个人大家庭的户主。我母亲说那两个人能凭空吵出一场争论，而那吵闹又会生出更多吵闹。那条街上每对父母都知道别人家的私事。我父亲从不提这些，整个故事我还是从我姑妈那儿听来的。"},"flower":{"tw":[["floral",4],["bloom",0],["bud",3],["develop",2],["tree",6],["prime",0],["daisy",3],["garden",6]],"en":"The flower show opens on the first Saturday of June. Every garden in the village brings something: one rose, one daisy, one strange plant in a pot. The floral tent is the biggest in the county. My aunt watches her buds for weeks; a flower that is not yet in bloom cannot win, and one past its prime cannot either. The tree by the gate develops its leaves late and loses them early. The judge looks at the colour first and the shape last, and he never hurries. The show closes at six and the tent is taken down the same evening.","zh":"花展六月的第一个周六开幕。村里每座园子都拿出点什么：一支玫瑰、一朵雏菊、一盆奇怪的植物。那座花卉帐篷是全县最大的。我姑妈守着花苞看了好几周；还没开的花赢不了，过了盛期的也赢不了。大门边那棵树发芽晚，落叶却早。"},"live":{"tw":[["liver",4],["experience",2],["board",3],["dead",1],["except",6],["hot",0],["camp",3],["alone",6],["last",0]],"en":"My uncle has lived in a camp near the river for ten years, mostly alone. He is not dead, though some of the men he worked with are. He says the only thing that makes a long stay bearable is experience: you learn which food is safe and which water is hot enough to drink. Except for the winter, he is out on the board path every morning. Doctors once told him his liver was weak, so he eats little meat and walks a lot. He wants to live in a real house last of all, but not yet.","zh":"我叔叔在河边的一个营地里住了十年，大多时候是一个人。他没死，虽然跟他一起干过活的人里有些已经不在了。他说，能让这种长住熬得下去的只有经验：你得知道哪些东西能吃，哪里的水烧热了才能喝。除了冬天，他每天早上都出门，走那条木板路。医生曾说他肝不好，所以他少吃肉、多走路。他说到最后还是想住进一间真正的房子，但不是现在。"},"empty":{"tw":[["abandon",0],["clear",3],["change",2],["fill",1],["inside",6],["discharge",0],["bleed",3],["leave",2],["room",6],["hollow",0]],"en":"The old factory was empty when we got there. Someone had left the gate open, and a clear wind blew through a broken window. We had come to change the locks and fill the holes in the floor. Inside, a great hollow tank stood against the wall where the water used to be stored. They had to discharge the last of it through a pipe, and a thin stream continued to bleed onto the concrete for an hour. I could not abandon the place; it was the room where my father worked. We would leave it standing, at least for one more year.","zh":"我们到的时候，那家老厂是空的。有人把大门敞着，一股清亮的风从破窗里穿过去。我们来是为了换锁，再把地板上的洞补上。屋里靠墙立着一个巨大的空罐子，从前就是在那儿储水的。剩下的水得从一根管子里排出去，细细的一股流在水泥地上淌了一个小时。我没法把这儿丢下不要；这是我父亲当年干活的车间。我们决定先让它立着，至少再留一年。"},"express":{"tw":[["carry",0],["drop",3],["mail",2],["local",1],["message",6],["state",0],["raise",3],["communicate",2],["service",6],["convey",2]],"en":"The local post office will not carry a parcel that is too heavy, so I had to express it instead. The clerk asked me to state the value and then to raise the box onto the scale. She said the mail service would get the message to my brother by Friday. I tried to convey how urgent it was, and she promised to drop it in the first van out. The old way of sending letters could not communicate such speed. I paid, took the receipt, and left feeling that the whole thing had gone well.","zh":"本地的邮局不收太重的包裹，所以我只好走快递。柜台的人让我报一下价值，再把箱子抬到秤上。她说邮件服务周五之前能把消息送到我哥哥手上。我想让她明白这事有多急，她答应把这箱子塞进第一班发走的车里。从前寄信的老法子根本传达不了这么快的速度。我付了钱，拿了收据，走的时候觉得整件事办得挺顺。"},"fall":{"tw":[["autumn",0],["break",3],["change",2],["rise",1],["end",6],["drop",3],["rain",3],["die",2],["since",6],["hang",0]],"en":"Since the end of summer, the leaves have begun to fall. Each autumn I watch them drop from the tall trees behind the house, and they hang in the wet air before they reach the ground. The change comes quickly here: one week it is warm, the next the rain will not stop. Prices rise, the shops break their old rules and close early, and a few small birds die in the cold. My mother says this is the finest time of year, when the garden falls quiet. It is only October, and already the wood box by the door is full.","zh":"入夏以来，叶子就开始落了。每年秋天我都看着它们从屋后那些大树上掉下来，落地之前先悬在潮湿的空气里。这里变天变得快：这一周还暖着，下一周雨就下个不停。物价往上涨，店家打破了老规矩提前关门，几只小鸟冻死了。我妈说这是一年里最好的时节，园子静下来的时候。才十月，门边那只木箱子已经装满了。"},"feed":{"tw":[["course",0],["waste",3],["move",2],["starve",1],["consume",6],["eat",0],["dine",3],["provide",2],["grow",6],["run",0]],"en":"My aunt runs a small farm and has to feed forty animals before she can feed herself. Of course the cost has gone up, and she refuses to waste a single sack of grain. Each morning she will move the sheep to a new field, then provide water for the cows and let the young ones run about. In winter there is little to eat, and the weakest may starve if the hay does not last. At night she will dine alone in the kitchen, proud that the whole place can grow and consume and still pay for itself.","zh":"我姑姑经营一个小农场，得先把四十头牲口喂饱，才轮到自己吃饭。成本当然涨了，她一袋粮食都不肯糟蹋。每天早上她把羊赶到新的一片地里，然后给牛添水，让小牛四处跑。冬天没什么可吃的，草料要是撑不到开春，最弱的那几头就可能饿死。晚上她一个人在厨房吃饭，很得意这块地方能种能养、还能自己养自己。"},"fill":{"tw":[["meet",0],["answer",3],["change",2],["empty",1],["extra",6],["satisfy",0],["close",3],["enough",2],["room",6],["fulfil",0]],"en":"We had to fill the hall before eight o'clock, but the room was still half empty when the band began. An extra row of chairs helped, and by the time the door had to close there was enough space for everyone. The manager said we could not satisfy a crowd like that with a small show, so he had to change the programme and answer a few angry phone calls. In the end we did meet the promise and fulfil the plan. I sat at the back and watched the seats fill one by one.","zh":"我们得在八点前把礼堂填满，可乐队开场时屋子还空着一半。加了一排椅子才管用，等到不得不关门的时候，位子已经够所有人坐了。经理说这种规模的观众，小节目是满足不了的，于是他改了节目单，还接了几个气冲冲的电话。最后我们总算兑现了承诺，把计划做成了。我坐在最后一排，看着座位一个个被填满。"},"find":{"tw":[["chance",0],["catch",3],["act",2],["lose",1],["how",6],["discover",0],["count",3],["change",2],["sure",6],["feel",3]],"en":"I had to find the key before my father came home, and I was not sure how to do it. There was a chance he had left it in the car, so I went out to look. I had to act quickly, count the minutes while I searched, and feel along every shelf. I did not want to lose my nerve or let the light change before I was finished. Then I began to discover small things: a torn ticket, a note, and at last the key itself. I managed to catch the door just as he turned into the road.","zh":"我必须在爸爸回家之前找到钥匙，可我不确定该怎么办。有可能他把它落在车里了，于是我就出去找。我得赶紧动手，一边找一边数着分钟，把每个架子都摸一遍。我不想在这期间慌了神，也不想等天光变了还没找完。后来我开始发现一些小东西：一张撕破的票、一张纸条，最后就是钥匙本身。他拐进这条路的时候，我刚好把门接住。"},"finish":{"tw":[["close",3],["break",3],["act",2],["start",1],["straight",6],["complete",0],["draw",3],["coat",2],["round",6],["end",3]],"en":"The painter said he would finish the room in three days, but the start was slow. He had to draw the shape of each window first, then work in a straight line down the wall. We would break for tea at eleven and close the door so the dust did not reach the hall. The first coat took a whole day; the second was quicker. At the end of the round he asked me to act as judge and look for any thin patch. It was complete by Friday, and the whole job turned out better than I had hoped.","zh":"油漆工说三天就能把这间屋子刷完，可开头很慢。他得先把每扇窗的形状描出来，再顺着墙面一笔直着往下刷。十一点我们会停下来喝茶，把门关上，免得灰飘到走廊里。第一遍漆刷了一整天，第二遍就快多了。这一轮收尾的时候，他让我当裁判，去找有没有刷薄的地方。到周五就全完工了，整件活儿比我想的还好。"},"follow":{"tw":[["watch",0],["carry",3],["act",2],["precede",1],["change",6],["observe",0],["chase",3],["check",2],["see",6],["trace",0]],"en":"A good guide will follow the old path and never act on guesswork. He will watch the sky, observe where the birds go, and check the marks on the trees. The men who precede him leave signs, and he can trace every one of them. If the wind should change, he must carry on without complaint and chase the last of the light. I have seen him do it a hundred times. You follow because you trust him, not because you can see the way yourself. The rest of us simply walk behind and try not to lose him.","zh":"好向导会跟着那条老路走，绝不凭猜行事。他会看天，观察鸟往哪儿飞，检查树上的记号。走在他前面的人留下标记，他能把每一个都追踪出来。风要是变了向，他也得一声不吭地往前走，追着最后一点天光。我见他这么干过一百回。你跟着他，是因为信得过他，不是因为你自个儿看得清路。我们这些剩下的人只管在后面走，尽量别跟丢。"},"foot":{"tw":[["base",0],["bed",3],["add",2],["head",1],["hole",6],["pick",0],["paw",3],["bottom",2],["inside",6],["infantry",0]],"en":"There was a hole in my boot, and by the end of the walk my foot was wet. The base of the hill is soft, so each step sank a little, and I had to pick my way between the stones. My dog ran ahead on a heavy paw, then stopped and put his head down at the bottom of a wall. Inside the old shed we found a bed of dry grass and a line of marks that looked like an army. My father said the infantry had camped there long ago, before the road was built. He added that his own feet still hurt from that winter.","zh":"我靴子上有个洞，走到最后脚全湿了。山脚下土很松，每一步都往下陷一点，我只得在石头之间挑着路走。我的狗用一只厚爪子跑在前面，忽然停下来，把头低在一堵墙脚下。在那间旧棚子里，我们找到一片干草铺的窝，还有一排看着像脚印的痕迹。我爸说很久以前、路还没修的时候，步兵在这儿扎过营。他又说他的脚到现在还记得那个冬天。"},"free":{"tw":[["rid",0],["clear",5],["issue",2],["confine",1],["without",6],["innocent",0],["cut",3],["pass",2],["allow",6],["loose",5]],"en":"The court set him free after nine months. He had been confined to a small cell without a window, and no one would allow him to see the papers in his own case. The judge said he was innocent, that the police had no right to cut him off from his family, and that the whole issue was a mistake. He walked out, let his shoulders go loose, and took a clear breath of morning air. He wanted only to be rid of the past and to pass through the gate like any other man.","zh":"九个月后，法庭把他放了。他先前被关在一间没有窗的小牢房里，谁也不让他看自己案子的卷宗。法官说他是无罪的，警方没有权利把他和家人隔开，说整件事就是个错误。他走出来，把肩膀松开，清清爽爽地吸了一口早晨的空气。他只想把过去甩掉，像个普通人一样从大门走出去。"},"freeze":{"tw":[["block",0],["ice",3],["act",2],["boil",1],["resume",6],["frost",3],["fixate",3],["change",2],["unless",6],["halt",0]],"en":"Unless the pipes are wrapped, the water in them will freeze on the first cold night. Last year the ice blocked the whole line and the heating had to halt for two days. My neighbour began to fixate on the weather report, watching for frost and for any change in the wind. We agreed to act together: he would boil water for the old man next door while I went to get salt. In the morning the thaw came, and the traffic could resume along the main road. For a week nothing moved, and we counted the days by the marks on the kitchen wall.","zh":"管子要是不包上，里头的水在第一个寒夜就会冻住。去年冰把整条管线堵死了，暖气不得不停了整整两天。我邻居开始盯着天气预报不放，一心等霜冻、等风向有什么变化。我们说好一起动手：他去给隔壁老人烧水，我去弄盐。早上化冻了，大路上的车又能走了。那一个星期什么也动不了，我们就在厨房墙上划道子数日子。"},"front":{"tw":[["face",3],["nose",3],["lie",2],["back",1],["inside",6],["look",0],["bow",3],["line",2],["behind",6],["breast",0]],"en":"The old house stands at the front of a narrow street, with a small garden behind it. Its face is grey, and the paint on the nose of each window has worn away. Inside, a long line of photographs hangs on the wall, and the ones at the back are almost white. My grandmother would look at them and bow her head a little. She said the house must not lie empty, that a family should live at its breast, close to the road, where everyone can see who comes and goes.","zh":"那栋老房子立在一条窄街的最前头，后面有个小园子。它的门面是灰的，每扇窗子凸出来的那块漆都磨掉了。屋里墙上挂着一长排照片，靠里的那些几乎白得看不清了。我奶奶会看着它们，微微低下头。她说这房子不能空着躺在那儿，一家人该住在它的胸口上，紧挨着大路，好让谁都看得见谁进谁出。"},"good":{"tw":[["dear",0],["basic",3],["advantage",2],["bad",1],["sure",6],["full",0],["better",3],["quality",2],["think",6],["near",0]],"en":"My grandfather always said that a good name is worth more than money. He kept the shop near the bridge for forty years and never once sold anything of poor quality. Of course it was hard to make a living, but he thought the basic advantage of the work was simple: people trusted him, and trust is a dear thing. When trade turned bad he did not complain. He was sure that if he stayed full of patience things would get better, and in the end they did. That, he said, was the whole of the matter.","zh":"我爷爷总说，好名声比钱值钱。他在桥边开那家铺子开了四十年，一回也没卖过差东西。谋生当然不容易，但他觉得这活儿最基本的好处很简单：人家信得过他，而信得过是很金贵的东西。生意变差的时候他也不抱怨。他认定只要耐着性子熬着，日子总会好起来，后来果然就好了。他说，事情的全部就是这个。"},"ground":{"tw":[["base",0],["build",3],["hit",2],["figure",1],["fire",6],["earth",3],["floor",3],["paint",2],["inside",6],["land",2]],"en":"The workers had to clear the ground before they could build anything. They hit a thick layer of clay at the base of the slope, and the figure on their plan had to be changed. Inside the fence the floor of the old shed was still there, with a door of green paint and the marks of an old fire on the wall. The land belonged to a family who had farmed it for a hundred years. Now a line of lorries carries away the earth and nothing will grow on that ground for a long time.","zh":"工人们得先把地清出来才能动工盖东西。他们在坡底下一头撞上厚厚一层黏土，图纸上的数字只得改了。围墙里面，那间旧棚子的地面还在，还有一扇刷绿漆的门和墙上的一个壁炉。这块地属于一家人，他们种了一百年。现在一队卡车把土一车车运走，那片地上很久都不会再长出什么来了。"},"hit":{"tw":[["reach",0],["bottom",3],["move",2],["miss",1],["run",6],["shoot",0],["cut",3],["touch",2],["double",6],["strike",0]],"en":"The batsman waited, watched the ball, and then hit it hard. The crowd rose as it began to reach the far side of the field, and the men on the boundary had to run. He did not miss once that afternoon, and twice he made the ball touch the top of the wall for a double. When the light began to go, the captain told him to cut the risk and stop trying to shoot at everything. He moved down the pitch slowly, took one last strike, and the ball rolled to the bottom of the bank.","zh":"击球手等着，盯着球，然后狠狠一击。球开始飞向场地那头，看台上的人都站起来了，边界上的几个球员只得跑起来。那天下午他一次也没落空，还有两回让球碰到墙顶，跑成两分。天光渐暗时，队长叫他别再冒风险，不要见什么都打。他慢慢地走下球道，最后一击，球滚到了坡底。"},"issue":{"tw":[["cut",0],["change",3],["store",2],["recall",1],["question",6],["matter",0],["check",3],["write",2],["whether",6],["return",0]],"en":"The manager had to recall a whole line of tins and issue a notice to every store in the district. The question was whether the fault came from the factory or from the long journey in the heat. He asked me to check the records and write a short report on the matter. There had been a change in the way the lids were cut, and nobody could say when it started. We had to return three hundred boxes to the plant. It was a small issue, but it cost us a month.","zh":"经理不得不召回一整批罐头，并向区里每家商店发一份通知。问题在于毛病出在工厂，还是出在炎热天气里那趟长途运输。他让我去核一下记录，就这件事写一份简短的报告。罐盖的裁切方式有过一次改动，谁也说不清是从什么时候开始的。我们得把三百箱货退回厂里。事情本身不大，却耗了我们一个月。"},"last":{"tw":[["close",0],["run",3],["measure",2],["first",1],["ago",6],["end",2],["wear",3],["rank",2],["since",6],["final",0]],"en":"My last summer at the school began long ago in the first week of June and ended in the middle of August. I had to run a mile every morning, and the coach would measure the time and write it on the board. Since the oldest boys always took the top rank, I never came close to them. By the final week my shoes had begun to wear through at the toe. On the last day the whole class stood in a line at the end of the field, and the headmaster said a few words that I have carried with me for a long time.","zh":"我在学校过的最后一个夏天，是从六月的第一周开始，到八月中结束的。每天早上我都得跑一英里，教练会量时间，再写在校牌上。因为最高名次总被年纪最大的那几个占着，我从来没能靠近他们。到了最后一周，我的鞋脚尖已经开始磨穿了。最后一天，全班在场地尽头站成一排，校长讲了几句话，那些话我一直记到今天。"},"law":{"tw":[["lawyer",4],["police",0],["force",2],["justice",6],["legal",4],["philosophy",2],["statute",6]],"en":"My cousin trained as a lawyer and now works for a small firm that takes cases the police will not touch. He says the law is not the same thing as justice, and that any statute can be read in two ways. The force of an old rule may last for a century after the reason for it is gone. At night he reads a little philosophy, because the questions he meets in court are older than any legal book. He tells me that most of what people call justice is really just care taken with details.","zh":"我表哥学的是法律，现在在一家小事务所做事，接的都是警方不愿沾的案子。他说法律和公正不是一回事，任何一条成文法都能有两种读法。一条旧规矩的效力，可能在它的道理早就没了之后还要撑上一百年。夜里他会读一点哲学，因为他在法庭上遇到的那些问题，比任何法学书都古老。他跟我说，人们嘴里的公正，多半不过是对细节的一点点用心。"},"leave":{"tw":[["allow",0],["pass",3],["change",2],["arrive",1],["stay",6],["forget",0],["remember",3],["lose",2],["return",6],["lead",3]],"en":"We had to leave the hotel before six, and the manager would not allow us to stay a minute longer. The train was due to arrive at half past, so we had to pass through the empty streets with our bags. My mother kept checking that she was not forgetting anything, and then, of course, she would remember something else. I was afraid we should lose the connection at the next station. But the change was easy, and by noon we had returned to the town that had led us out thirty years before.","zh":"我们六点前就得离开旅馆，经理一分钟都不肯让我们多留。火车半点到，所以我们只好拎着箱子穿过空荡荡的街道。我妈一遍遍检查自己有没有忘东西，然后当然又想起来了别的。我担心我们在下一站会误了换乘。可换车很顺利，中午的时候，我们已经回到了三十年前带我们离开的那座小镇。"},"level":{"tw":[["charge",0],["high",3],["state",2],["raise",1],["current",6],["flat",0],["low",3],["talk",2],["below",6],["floor",3]],"en":"The engineer stood on the floor of the hall and checked the level of the water in the tank. It was still low, only a metre below the mark, so he had to raise the pipe and let the current run for an hour. He did not want to charge the whole system again, because the pressure was already high. His talk with the manager had been short and flat: either the state of the pumps improved, or the building would have to close for a week. In the end he found a simple answer and wrote it down on the wall.","zh":"工程师站在大厅的地面上，查看水箱里的水位。水还很低，离刻线只差一米，所以他得把管子抬高，让水流上一个小时。他不想再给整个系统充一次压，因为压力本来就高。他跟经理那番谈话又短又平淡：要么水泵的状况好转，要么这栋楼就得关一个星期。最后他想出个简单的办法，把它写在了墙上。"},"lie":{"tw":[["rest",0],["back",3],["position",2],["sit",1],["hide",6],["consist",0],["charge",3],["exist",2],["else",6],["dwell",0]],"en":"The old dog likes to lie in the same place every evening, at the back of the kitchen where nobody else goes. His position never changes; he will rest there for hours and only sit up when he hears a car. I asked the vet whether any trouble might hide behind such quiet habits, and she said that a dog's health can consist of very little: food, warmth, and a good place to sleep. She told me not to charge him with anything more, and to let him dwell in his own corner as long as he exists.","zh":"那条老狗每天傍晚都要躺在一个固定的地方，就是厨房里头谁也去不到的角落。它的位置从不改变；它能在那里歇上好几个钟头，只有听见车声才坐起来。我问兽医，这么安静的习性背后会不会藏着什么毛病。她说狗的健康其实可以由很少的东西组成：吃食、暖和，再加一个睡觉的好地方。她叫我别再给它加什么负担，让它就在自己的角落里待着，活一天算一天。"},"like":{"tw":[["care",0],["love",3],["see",2],["dislike",1],["look",6],["same",5],["please",3],["desire",2],["well",6],["wish",0]],"en":"My sister and I look exactly the same, and we like the same things. But she does not care for cold mornings, and I dislike them even more. As you wish, she said one day, but I should love a walk by the river. I could see she was not well, so I did not please her. Her one desire was a hot drink and a long rest. I looked at her face and thought how much alike we were, and how little it mattered. We were like two cups thrown by the same hand, and neither of us could be happy alone.","zh":"我和姐姐长得一模一样，喜欢的东西也一样。可她受不了冷天早晨，我比她更讨厌。有一天她说：随你吧，不过我倒是很想沿河走一走。我看得出她身子不舒服，就没顺着她。她唯一的念头是一杯热饮和好好歇一会儿。我看着她那张脸，心想我们俩多像啊，而这又多么不重要。我们像同一双手捏出来的两只杯子，谁单独一个都不会快活。"},"love":{"tw":[["bed",0],["romance",3],["like",2],["hate",1],["dream",6],["dear",0],["worship",3],["object",2],["mind",6],["bang",0]],"en":"My grandmother says she did not fall in love with my grandfather at first sight; she simply liked him and went on liking him. There was no romance in the little flat where they began, only one bed and a window over the yard. I hate to say it, she told me, but after fifty years the dear old man is still the first object in my mind. She keeps his picture by her bed and worships the ground he walks on. She has a dream that they will meet again. Then she banged the kettle down and laughed at herself.","zh":"我奶奶说，她对我爷爷不是一见钟情；她只是一开始喜欢他，然后就一直喜欢下去。他们起头的那间小公寓里没什么浪漫，只有一张床和一扇朝院子的窗。她跟我说：我不愿意这么说，可过了五十年，这个老头子还是我心里头头一件放着的事。她把他照片摆在床边，把他走过的地都当圣地。她还做着再见到他的梦。说完她把水壶往下一磕，自己笑了。"},"end":{"tw":[["close",3],["break",3],["change",2],["begin",1],["next",6],["death",3],["complete",3],["start",6],["finish",0]],"en":"On his last day at the mill my father stayed until the end of the night shift. There was no break, and no one asked for one. He had begun there at eighteen and finished at sixty-two, and in all those years the only real change was the new machines. At close of day the manager shook his hand. Then, at the start of the next week, he found that work was not everything. The death of a friend that autumn had taught him that. Something was complete, and another thing was just beginning. He walked home slowly in the dark, past the empty yard and the locked gate.","zh":"父亲在厂里的最后一天，一直干到夜班结束。中间没歇，也没人提。他十八岁进厂，六十二岁收工，这么多年里唯一真正变了的就是那些新机器。收工时经理跟他握了手。到了下一个星期开头，他才发现干活并不是一切。那年秋天一个朋友的去世让他明白了这个道理。一件事算完了，另一件事才刚刚开始。他摸着黑慢慢走回家，路过空荡荡的院子和锁着的大门。"},"excuse":{"tw":[["pardon",0],["plead",3],["note",2],["mistake",6],["apology",0],["alibi",3],["forgive",2],["wrong",6],["justify",0]],"en":"The boy stood at the door with a note in his hand and asked the teacher to pardon him for being late. It was a mistake, he said, and he began to plead his case. His excuse was that the bus had broken down. He even had an alibi: two friends who had waited with him. She read the note twice and put it down. There was no apology for the noise he had made the day before. She said she would forgive him this time, but that he could not justify the same thing twice. Nothing was wrong with the story, only with him.","zh":"男孩站在门口，手里捏着一张条子，请老师原谅他迟到。他说是自己的错，接着就开始辩。他找的理由是公交车坏在了半路。他甚至还有人为他作证：两个跟他一起等的同学。老师把条子读了两遍，放在桌上。他对自己前一天闹出的那阵动静，一句道歉也没有。她说这回可以原谅他，但同样的事没有第二遍的道理。故事本身没毛病，毛病在他身上。"},"experience":{"tw":[["feel",3],["burn",3],["change",2],["physical",6],["live",0],["die",3],["content",2],["good",6],["see",0]],"en":"My grandmother used to say that a long life is only a long experience. She had lived through a war, lost a brother, and seen a whole street fall down and change. In her last years the work in the garden was too physical for her, but she would not stop. She liked to feel the sun on her back. She had one burn on her arm from a hot pan, and she showed it to me as if it were a medal. She was content with small things. A year later she died, and I still think of her. She was good at that, at being happy.","zh":"奶奶常说，活得久不过就是一段长的经历。她经过一场战争，失去过一个兄弟，也亲眼见过整条街塌掉、变了样。最后那几年，园子里的活对她身子来说太重了，可她不肯停。她喜欢太阳晒在背上的感觉。她胳膊上有一块被热锅烫的伤，拿给我看的时候像在展示一枚奖章。小事就能让她满足。一年后她走了，我到现在还常想起她。她这个人，很会高兴。"},"family":{"tw":[["class",0],["couple",3],["unit",2],["father",6],["home",0],["sex",3],["relative",2],["mother",6],["house",3]],"en":"Ours was a family of six in a house too small for a class of that size. My father worked nights, my mother kept the accounts, and a couple of relatives lived with us for two winters. When the school sent a form home, it asked for the name, the age and the sex of each child, and my mother filled it in without a word. She said a family is not a unit of the state; it is only people who stay. I did not understand her then. Now that both of them are gone, I do. She wrote our surname slowly, in her careful hand.","zh":"我们家六口人，挤在一栋小得装不下这样一个班的房子里。父亲上夜班，母亲管账，有两三个亲戚跟我们一起住过两个冬天。学校把表格发到家里，上面要填每个孩子的姓名、年龄和性别，母亲一句话没说就填了。她说家不是国家的一个单位，只是几个肯留下来的人。那时我不懂她这话。如今他们两个都不在了，我懂了。她一笔一笔慢慢写下我们的姓，字写得很仔细。"},"farm":{"tw":[["grow",0],["carry",3],["collect",2],["mill",6],["raise",0],["ranch",3],["work",2],["plant",6],["produce",0]],"en":"My uncle runs a small farm near the old mill. In spring he has to plant and to grow enough food for the winter, and in autumn he will collect what the fields produce. He raises a few cows and, on the other side of the road, his brother has a ranch where they raise horses. Every morning he must carry water out to the animals before the work begins. He says a farm is not land. It is a habit. He has never wanted anything else, and he has never once been away from it. The house smells of wood smoke and old bread all year.","zh":"我叔在老磨坊旁边经营一小块农场。春天他得下种，种出够一冬吃的粮食；秋天他要收地里长出来的东西。他养了几头奶牛，路另一头他兄弟有个牧场，养马。每天早上开工之前，他得先把水挑出去喂牲口。他说农场不是一块地，是一种习惯。他从没想过要别的，也从没离开过这里一天。那屋子一年到头都是柴火和旧面包的味道。"},"fear":{"tw":[["care",0],["scare",3],["worry",2],["anger",6],["concern",0],["alarm",3],["respect",2],["blame",6],["awe",0]],"en":"Nobody in the village felt fear of the old shepherd, only a kind of awe. He carried a stick and a dog, and he did not care what people said about him. When a dog began to scare the sheep, he would stand still, and the animal would stop. His only concern was the weather. He used to say that worry is a tax you pay before the bill comes. Once I saw anger in his face, when a boy threw a stone. He did not blame the child. He just raised his arm, and there was alarm in every eye on the road. But no one ever lost respect for him.","zh":"村里没人怕那个老牧羊人，只有一种敬畏。他拿着一根棍子，带着一条狗，别人怎么说他都不在乎。有条狗开始吓羊的时候，他就站住不动，那畜生也就停下了。他唯一在意的是天气。他常说，担心是在账还没来之前就先交的税。有一次我看见他脸上有了怒气，是有个孩子扔石头。他没有怪那孩子，只是抬了抬胳膊，路上每一双眼睛里都是惊慌。可是谁也没有失掉对他的敬重。"},"fellow":{"tw":[["associate",2],["date",3],["friend",2],["young",6],["familiar",0],["dog",3],["man",2],["veteran",6],["mate",0]],"en":"The fellow who kept the shop was an old veteran with a bad leg. He was familiar with every man on the street and every dog in it. A young friend of mine used to sit at his counter for hours. They were mates, in a way, though one was eighty and the other sixteen. His only associate in business was a cousin who came on the same date each month to bring the money. I never heard him call anyone by a title. He called them all by name, and that was enough. He died the winter after I left, and the shop closed with him.","zh":"开那家小店的伙计是个腿有旧伤的退伍老兵。街上每个人、每条狗他都认得。我有个年轻朋友，常在他柜台边一坐几个钟头。他们算是哥们儿，尽管一个八十，一个十六。他生意上唯一的合伙人是位表亲，每月同一天来送钱。我从没听他用头衔叫过谁，都是直呼其名，这就够了。我走后的那个冬天他走了，小店也跟着关了。"},"field":{"tw":[["study",0],["court",3],["answer",2],["team",6],["subject",0],["flat",3],["choose",2],["run",6],["discipline",0]],"en":"The field where we played was flat and bare, with a court drawn on the ground in white chalk. Our team had to choose a captain before the match, and nobody could answer at first. The study of the game was my uncle's whole subject; he had a discipline about it that we never had. He would run up and down the side with us until it was dark. I remember the field more clearly than the games. I can still see the grass, the lines, and the long shadow of the goal. It is a car park for the new office now.","zh":"我们踢球的那块场地又平又空，地上用白粉画出一个球场。比赛前我们队得选一个队长，起初谁也说不出话来。对这门球艺的研究是我叔的全部功课，他在这上头有种我们从来没有的严格。他会跟我们一起沿着边线跑上跑下，跑到天黑。那块场地我记得比比赛还清楚。我到现在还能看见那片草、那些线，还有球门拉出的长影子。如今那儿是新办公楼的一个停车场。"},"fight":{"tw":[["press",0],["box",3],["advertise",2],["bring",6],["push",0],["settle",3],["try",2],["face",6],["battle",0]],"en":"There was a fight behind the pub on Saturday night, and it took two men to settle it. One of them boxed badly; he kept his face open and took a blow on the nose. The other would only push, never strike. The owner of the shop next door came out to bring them apart. He did not advertise it, but he had been a soldier, and he had seen a real battle once. He did not press charges. He just told them to try again in the morning, when they were sober, and they did. Nobody was hurt enough to call a doctor.","zh":"星期六晚上酒馆后面有人打架，两个人才能拉开。其中一个拳法很糟，脸敞着，鼻子上挨了一下。另一个只是推，从不出拳。隔壁铺子的老板出来把他们分开。这事他不张扬，可他当过兵，真见过一回战场。他没有去告谁。他只叫他们等早上酒醒了再试一次，他们真就照办了。谁也没伤到要请大夫。"},"film":{"tw":[["movie",0],["roll",3],["record",2],["documentary",6],["picture",0],["object",2],["feature",3],["comic",6],["shoot",0]],"en":"My father had one roll of film from the year I was born, and he would shoot a picture of the same street every spring. He kept every object in the house in its place, and every record on the shelf in order. He loved a good movie, but he never liked a comic one. There was a short documentary about the old market that used his film, and it was the only feature my mother ever watched twice. He said a photograph is not a memory. It is only proof that you were there. I have the camera still, and no film for it.","zh":"父亲有从我出生那年留下的一卷胶卷，每年春天他都去拍一张同一条街。屋里每样东西他都摆在自己该在的位置，架子上的每张唱片也按次序放好。他喜欢好电影，可从来不爱看滑稽的。有一部讲老市场的短片用了他的胶片，那是母亲唯一看过两遍的片子。他说，照片不是记忆，它只证明你当时在那儿。那台相机我还留着，只是没胶卷了。"},"first":{"tw":[["low",0],["former",3],["position",2],["last",1],["early",6],["start",0],["threshold",3],["gear",2],["offset",0]],"en":"At the start of the race my brother was in the first position, and he held it for the whole first lap. Then his gear slipped and he dropped to the low side of the pack. The former winner, who had started early, was behind him now. He crossed the threshold of the last corner and did not look back. That small offset in the time was enough. He came in second, and he was happier than he had been the year he won. He had trained on that hill all winter, alone, before anyone else was up. After the race he sat on the kerb and drank water slowly.","zh":"比赛一开始，我哥就排在第一位，第一圈一直守着。后来变速器一打滑，他掉到了队伍靠后的位置。那个早出发的前冠军这会儿在他后头。他冲过最后一个弯角前的界线，没有回头。时间上那一点小小的偏差就够了。他跑了个第二，比当年拿第一那年还高兴。整个冬天他一个人在那道坡上练，天没亮就起来。赛后他坐在路沿上，慢慢喝水。"},"fit":{"tw":[["agree",0],["hang",3],["shape",2],["better",6],["check",0],["look",3],["adapt",2],["sure",6],["meet",2]],"en":"The coat did not fit my sister, though she liked its shape and cut. In the shop she had to check it three times before she would agree. The woman there kept a mirror hanging behind the door, and my sister would look at herself and then look again. She was not sure about the length. In the end, she asked them to adapt it a little, a better plan than sending it back. She had to meet the tailor the next week. She said a thing can be made right, and that was why she never returned anything. The tailor only laughed at that.","zh":"那件外套我姐穿着不合身，尽管她喜欢那版型和剪裁。在店里她得来回看三遍才肯点头。那女的在门后挂了面镜子，我姐照了又照。她拿不准长短。最后她请他们改一改——这比退回去强。她得下星期去见裁缝。她说，东西是可以改好的，就为这个她从来不退货。裁缝听了只是笑。"},"floor":{"tw":[["base",0],["startle",3],["beat",2],["room",6],["deck",0],["loft",3],["control",2],["window",6],["dump",0]],"en":"The floor of the old room was bare wood, and the base of every wall was dark with age. A loud knock at the window startled me, and my heart began to beat fast. Up in the loft above, my brother was moving boxes, and his boots shook the deck of boards over my head. He had no control over his temper in those days. He would dump everything on the floor and leave it there. I stood at the door and said nothing. Twenty years later I bought that house, and I put in a new floor. It is a plain floor, and I like it.","zh":"那间老屋的地板是没上漆的木头，每面墙的墙根都黑得发旧。窗户上一声重响把我吓了一跳，心开始猛跳。楼上阁楼里，我哥在搬箱子，靴子踩得头顶那层板子直响。那些年他管不住自己的脾气，什么都往地上一扔就不管了。我站在门口一句话没说。二十年后我把那栋房子买了下来，换了新地板。地板很素净，我喜欢。"},"fly":{"tw":[["wing",0],["break",3],["change",2],["sail",6],["flee",0],["escape",3],["hit",2],["cruise",6],["pilot",0]],"en":"The fly came in through the open window and could not find its way out again. It would hit the glass and then change direction, and its wing made a small dry sound. My father, who had been a pilot, watched it for a while from his chair. He said that a bird can sail on the wind, and a man can cruise over a whole country, but a small thing like this can only flee or break. Then he opened the door wide and let it escape. He never killed anything in the house, not even a fly. That was one of the last things he taught me.","zh":"那只苍蝇从开着的窗户飞进来，怎么也找不着出去的路。它撞一下玻璃，换个方向再撞，翅膀发出很轻的干响。当过飞行员的父亲在椅子上看了一会儿。他说，鸟能借风滑行，人能驾机飞过一整个国家，可这么小的东西只能逃，或者撞断。然后他把门大敞开，放它出去了。屋里他从没弄死过什么，连一只苍蝇也没有。那是他教我的最后几件事之一。"},"force":{"tw":[["draw",0],["moment",3],["act",2],["military",6],["drive",3],["nose",3],["cause",2],["command",6],["power",0]],"en":"The force of the wind that night was enough to move a truck. It began to draw the door open, and for a moment nobody could close it. My neighbour, an old military man, took command at once. He told us to act and not to talk, and we pushed back with all our power. The wind had the drive of a train and hit the house nose first, like something alive. It was the cause of the flood two days later. I have never since felt so small in front of weather. The roof came off in one piece.","zh":"那一夜风的力道足以推动一辆卡车。它开始把门往外抽，有一阵子谁也关不上。我邻居是个老兵，他立刻接了手。他叫我们动手别说话，我们使出全副气力往回顶。那风像火车一样有劲，正对着房子撞上来，像是活的。两天后那场洪水就是它引起的。从那以后，我在天气面前再没觉得自己这么小过。屋顶整块被掀了下来。"},"game":{"tw":[["back",0],["catch",3],["bet",2],["season",6],["halt",0],["rabbit",3],["play",2],["match",6],["plot",0]],"en":"Every season the men in the village play the same game in the back room of the pub. One of them will bet on the first card and then lose it. My uncle had a plot of land behind his house where he once kept a rabbit hut. When the game came to a halt at midnight, they would stop the match and walk out slowly. Somebody would always catch the last bus. I used to sit under the table as a boy and watch their faces. In winter the room was cold and the window ran with water.","zh":"每年这个季节，村里的男人都在酒馆后屋玩同一种牌。总有人第一张牌就下注，然后输掉。我叔家后面有一小块地，以前搭过一个养兔子的棚。半夜牌局一停，他们就收了这一场，慢慢往外走。总有人赶得上末班车。小时候我常坐在桌子底下，看他们脸上的神情。冬天那屋子冷，玻璃上全是水。"},"get":{"tw":[["arrive",0],["break",3],["change",2],["sure",6],["beat",0],["buy",3],["experience",2],["want",6],["begin",0]],"en":"You could not get a seat on the early bus unless you arrived before seven. That was the first thing I learned, before I had any experience of the city at all. I had to buy a monthly ticket and be sure to keep it dry. On the day the engine began to break down, the driver would beat the panel with his hand, and nothing would change. I did not want to be late, so I walked. I got there in fifty minutes. After that I never took the bus again. The walk was long, and I liked it.","zh":"早班车你要是七点前不到，就抢不上座。这是我头一条学会的事，那时我对这座城市还毫无经验。我得买月票，还得保证别把它弄湿。发动机开始出毛病的那天，司机会用手砸仪表板，什么也不会变。我不想迟到，就走路。五十分钟到。从那以后我再没坐过那趟车。路很长，我却喜欢。"},"give":{"tw":[["afford",0],["allow",3],["accept",2],["need",6],["break",3],["deal",3],["change",2],["want",6],["feed",0]],"en":"My mother would give away anything she could not afford to keep. She would never allow a thing to sit unused in the house. If a neighbour needed a coat, she would accept nothing for it. Then, at the end of the deal, she would want to feed them before they left. She had a break in her voice when she spoke about the war, and a change would come over her face. There was nothing I could give her back. That is the part I still cannot manage. She died in March, in a small room full of white flowers.","zh":"我妈手里留不住东西，凡是养不起的，她都送人。她从不让一样东西在屋里搁着不用。邻居要是缺件外套，她什么也不收。事情办到最后，她还想留人家吃顿饭再走。提起那场战争，她声音里会有一下停顿，脸上也会起变化。我没什么能还给她。这一点我到现在也做不好。她三月里走的，在一间摆满白花的小屋里。"},"go":{"tw":[["break",3],["blow",3],["act",2],["want",6],["die",0],["check",3],["change",2],["sure",6],["fit",0]],"en":"The old pump had to go on working through the summer, or the whole garden would die. My father would check it every evening and be sure the belt was tight. He did not want to act too soon or too late, and he would not change a part that still fit. Then one night the handle began to break, and with a single blow the thing stopped. Water went everywhere. He stood there in the wet grass and laughed, which was not like him at all. A new pump came a week later. I remember the sound it made when it stopped.","zh":"那台老水泵得整个夏天一直转，不然满园子的东西都得死。父亲每天傍晚都去查看，确认皮带是紧的。他不肯动得太早或太晚，也不肯换掉还合用的零件。后来有天夜里，把手开始裂，就那么一下，机器停了。水淌了一地。他站在湿草里笑了，那一点也不像他。一星期后新泵来了。它停住时那声响我还记得。"},"grow":{"tw":[["farm",0],["carry",3],["change",2],["mature",6],["raise",0],["cut",3],["increase",2],["shrink",6],["rise",0]],"en":"On the farm my grandfather would grow the same three crops for fifty years, and he did not change them once. He had to carry the water himself until the pipes came. He would raise the young plants in boxes and cut the old trees back each spring. When the price of grain began to rise, his small plot seemed to increase in value, though his own share did not. He watched the fruit mature and then watched it shrink in the dry weeks. Carry, he said, and wait. That is what it is. I did not understand him then. I do now.","zh":"在农场，我爷爷五十年就种那三样庄稼，一次也没换过。水管接来之前，他得自己挑水。每年春天他把幼苗养在箱子里，把老树剪一剪。粮价开始往上涨的时候，他那一小块地看着是值钱了，可分到他手里的那份没变。他眼看着果子熟起来，又眼看着它们在干燥的几周里缩下去。他说：就挑着，等着，事情就是这样。那时我不懂他。现在我懂了。"},"handle":{"tw":[["address",0],["field",3],["control",2],["need",6],["care",0],["nurse",3],["touch",2],["without",6],["cover",0]],"en":"The handle of the ward door was worn smooth by years of hands. A nurse came out and asked for the address of the family, and I gave the one in the field beyond the river. My mother needed care at night, and someone had to touch her hand now and then so she would not feel alone. She could not control her own voice any more. There was a cover over the window, and without it the room was too bright. I stood there and did not know where to put myself. The handle was the last thing I touched.","zh":"病房门上的把手被无数只手磨得发亮。一位护士出来问家属的地址，我报的是河那边地里的那一处。母亲夜里需要人照料，得有人时不时碰一下她的手，让她不觉得孤单。她已经控制不住自己的声音了。窗户上有块遮布，没有它屋里太亮。我站在那儿，不知道把手往哪儿放。我最后碰到的是那个把手。"},"hang":{"tw":[["fall",0],["suspend",3],["drop",2],["shed",6],["dangle",3],["fit",2],["composite",6],["flow",0],["attend",0]],"en":"A lamp used to hang from the beam in my father's shed, and it would dangle a little whenever the wind came through. In autumn the leaves would fall, and one long thread of spider silk would suspend a single drop of rain above the door. He had a composite picture on the wall there, made of a hundred small photographs, and it did not fit the room at all. I had to attend to it when the glass broke. Water would flow down the inside of the wall after rain. He never fixed any of it. The shed came down with the house.","zh":"父亲棚子里从前梁上挂着一盏灯，风一吹进来它就轻轻晃。秋天叶子会落，一根长长的蛛丝会把一滴雨悬在门上头。那面墙上有一张拼起来的画，是一百张小照片拼的，跟那间屋子一点也不配。玻璃碎了的时候，得我去照应。下雨后水会顺着墙里侧往下流。这些他一样也没修过。棚子后来跟着那房子一起拆了。"},"hear":{"tw":[["discover",3],["catch",3],["concentrate",2],["tell",6],["listen",0],["incline",3],["probe",2],["answer",6],["see",0]],"en":"From my room I could hear the river, and if I held still I could catch the sound of a boat far off. I had to concentrate to tell one from the other. In the mornings I would listen for my father's step on the stairs, and I would incline my head towards the door. He never liked to be asked a direct question; he would probe the matter from the side and then not answer at all. I did not discover until much later that he had been ill that whole winter. Now I see the house in my sleep, and I still hear things in it.","zh":"从我屋里能听见那条河，要是屏住不动，还能听出远处一条船的声音。得集中注意力才分得清哪个是哪个。早上我会听着父亲的脚步声上楼，把头往门那边偏一偏。他不喜欢被直接问，总是从侧面探一探，然后干脆不回答。很久以后我才发现，那一整个冬天他都在生病。如今我在梦里还能看见那栋房子，还能听见里面的动静。"},"help":{"tw":[["serve",2],["care",3],["better",2],["bring",6],["service",0],["comfort",3],["support",2],["need",6],["aid",0]],"en":"When my aunt could no longer care for herself, the family had to choose between a private nurse and the public service. The clinic would serve her at home, and a young woman came twice a day to help. She would bring hot food and, better than that, she brought comfort. My aunt needed very little in the way of aid, only someone to support her arm on the stairs. I used to sit with her and read, and she would say that help is not a favour. It is a habit you learn. She died at home, in her own bed.","zh":"等我姑妈自己照顾不了自己的时候，家里得在私人雇的护士和公家的服务之间做选择。诊所可以上门，一个年轻女人一天来两趟帮忙。她带来热饭，比这更好的是带来了安慰。姑妈要的帮衬很少，只是上下楼时有人扶一把胳膊。我常坐在她那儿读书给她听，她总说：帮忙不是人情，是学会的一种习惯。她是在家里、在自己床上走的。"},"hold":{"tw":[["admit",3],["arrange",3],["continue",2],["meet",6],["agree",0],["call",3],["control",2],["bring",6],["bear",3]],"en":"The manager had to hold the meeting in the small office at the back. She would admit no one before nine, and she could not bear to be late herself. She had arranged the chairs in a circle so everyone could see the others. We had to agree on the price before we could continue. Then she had to call the supplier and bring the matter up again. I watched her hold her temper for an hour without a break. Later she told me that control is not a gift. It is a decision you make every morning. I still hear her voice when I have to wait.","zh":"经理只能在后头那间小办公室里开会。九点之前她谁也不放进去，自己也受不了迟到。她把椅子摆成一圈，好让每个人都看得见别人。价钱谈定之前，我们没法往下走。接着她得给供货商打电话，把这事重新提一遍。我看着她一个小时都没发火。后来她跟我说，克制不是天赋，是每天早上都要做的一个决定。要等的时候，我还能听见她的声音。"},"hole":{"tw":[["fix",0],["cup",3],["hit",2],["putt",6],["mess",0],["eye",3],["mouth",2],["bunker",6],["jam",0]],"en":"The hole on the fourth green was the worst on the course, and it took me three putts to get the ball near the cup. My first hit went straight into a bunker. My friend did not say a word; he just kept his eye on the ball and closed his mouth. The whole thing was a mess, and I had no idea how to fix it. A jam of players waited behind us. I picked up the ball with the club and laughed. It was the last time I ever tried to play this game. My friend never asked me again.","zh":"第四洞那个洞是全场最糟的，我推了三杆才把球推近洞口。第一杆直接打进了沙坑。朋友一句话没说，只是眼睛盯着球，闭着嘴。整件事一团糟，我根本不知道怎么补救。后面还堵着一堆打球的人。我用杆把球捡起来，笑了。那是我最后一次试着打这玩意儿。朋友后来再没叫过我。"},"honour":{"tw":[["observe",0],["letter",3],["accept",2],["occasion",6],["respect",0],["glory",3],["recognize",2],["medal",6],["award",0]],"en":"The medal came by post, in a plain envelope with a short letter inside. It was, he said, the only honour he had ever wanted, and he would not accept any praise for it. On such an occasion my father would say only that the award belonged to the men who were not there. We all had to observe his silence and say nothing. Later, at the small dinner, the old men stood up to recognize him, and there was a good deal of glory in the room that night. I have kept the medal. Respect, he said, is not something you can carry home.","zh":"奖章是邮寄来的，一只素净的信封里夹着一封短信。他说，这是他一辈子唯一想要的荣誉，他不肯为它接受任何称赞。遇上这种场合，父亲只会说，这奖该属于那些不在场的人。我们都得安静着，什么也不说。后来在那顿小饭局上，几个老人站起来认他，那晚上的屋里很有些光彩。奖章我留着。他说，敬重这东西，你带不回家。"},"hope":{"tw":[["promise",0],["rainbow",3],["plan",2],["despair",1],["bring",6],["trust",0],["wish",2],["chance",6],["desire",2]],"en":"After the flood our only hope was the small plan my uncle had written on the back of an envelope. He had made a promise to the village that he would not leave, and he kept it. There was a rainbow over the water on the third morning, and he said that was a good sign, though none of us had any trust in signs. I began to wish I had his calm. The chance of a good harvest that year was small, and there were days of real despair. But his desire to stay never moved. He would bring us bread from the next town.","zh":"洪水过后，我们唯一的指望就是叔叔写在信封背面的那份小计划。他跟村里许过诺，说他不会走，他做到了。第三天早上水面上有道彩虹，他说这是好兆头，可我们谁也不信兆头。我开始盼着自己能有他那样的镇定。那年收成好的机会很小，也有过真正绝望的日子。但他要留下的心从没动过。他会从邻镇给我们带面包回来。"},"hunt":{"tw":[["run",0],["drive",3],["club",2],["kill",6],["search",2],["rabbit",3],["chase",2],["wolf",6],["trace",0]],"en":"The hunt began at dawn, when the men would drive the rabbits out of the long grass towards the line. My grandfather never used a club. He would run with the dogs and then stand still and search the ground for a trace. A wolf had been seen near the wood that year, and it had taken two lambs. He said he would not kill anything he did not need. The chase was the part he loved, not the end of it. I followed him once, and I was too slow. He just laughed and told me to stay home.","zh":"天一亮就开始打猎，男人们把兔子从长草里往这一线赶。爷爷从不用棍子。他跟着狗跑，然后站住，在地上找痕迹。那年树林边出现过一条狼，叼走了两只羊羔。他说用不着的东西他不杀。他要的是追赶本身，不是结局。有一回我跟着他，太慢了。他只是笑笑，叫我待在家里。"},"hurry":{"tw":[["rush",0],["run",3],["act",2],["bother",6],["speed",2],["dash",3],["travel",2],["wait",6],["haste",0]],"en":"There is no need to hurry, my mother would say, whenever we were late. She would never rush, and she would not let us run in the street. In her view, haste was the reason most things went wrong: you act too fast and then you have to wait twice as long. She did not bother about the clock at all. She would travel with a small bag, and at the station she would walk at her own speed. Once I saw her dash for a train. She made it, and she did not even breathe hard. That is the only time I remember.","zh":"我们快迟到的时候，我妈总说：用不着赶。她从不慌，也不让我们在街上跑。在她看来，事情办砸多半是因为急：动手太快，后来就得等两倍的时间。她根本不在乎钟点。出门她只带一个小包，在车站按自己的速度走。有一回我看见她冲着一趟火车跑过去。她赶上了，气都没喘。我就记得那么一次。"},"insure":{"tw":[["check",0],["card",3],["protect",2],["incentive",6],["control",3],["doom",3],["guarantee",2],["ensure",6],["cover",3]],"en":"The man who came to insure the shop had to check every room and fill in a card for each one. He said the cover would protect us against fire and flood, though it could guarantee nothing about the street itself. His only incentive, he said, was the small sum he earned on each contract. There was no way to control the wind that came off the hill. My father signed anyway, and in a strange way it took the doom out of the winter. To ensure one more year, he said, is worth the money. The shop is still there.","zh":"来给铺子上保险的那个人把每间屋都查了一遍，一间填一张卡。他说这份保障能保我们不怕火灾和洪水，但街上本身的事它保证不了。他说自己唯一的动力就是每份合同上赚的那点小钱。从山上刮下来的风是管不住的。我父亲还是签了，奇怪的是，这一下把那个冬天的晦气拿掉了不少。他说，能再保一年，这钱就值。铺子现在还在。"},"interest":{"tw":[["concern",3],["right",3],["power",2],["credit",6],["worry",0],["absorb",3],["share",2],["term",6],["occupy",0]],"en":"The small shop occupied the corner of our street for forty years. When the owner died, the question of interest on the credit he had given came up at once, and nobody wanted to talk about it. My mother had a share of the place, on paper at least, and her only concern was that the right people should not lose money. The bank had the power to change the terms, and the worry of it absorbed her whole summer. She read every letter twice. I never once saw her cry. She was that kind of woman, and I am not.","zh":"那家小店在街角开了四十年。店主去世后，他生前赊出去那笔钱该算多少利息，这问题马上摆了上来，可谁都不愿意提。那地方我母亲是有一份的，至少在纸面上有，她唯一在意的是别让该得的人吃亏。银行有权改条件，这桩心事占了她整个夏天。每封信她都读两遍。我一次也没见她哭过。她就是那样的人，我不是。"},"job":{"tw":[["business",0],["game",3],["book",2],["better",6],["line",0],["position",3],["work",2],["good",6],["problem",0]],"en":"My first job was in a small business that sold school books. The manager gave me one line to look after and told me to keep the shelf in good order. It was not a game, she said, though the rules were much the same. My position there was the lowest in the building, and the work was dull. But it was better than waiting at home, and I learned how to deal with a problem without making it worse. I stayed for three years. When I left, she gave me a book. I still have it, and I still cannot read it.","zh":"我的头一份工作是在一家卖教科书的小公司。经理交给我一条货架，叫我保持整齐。她说这不是玩游戏，可规矩差不多。我在那儿的位置是整栋楼里最低的，活儿也闷。可总比在家等着强，我也学会了怎么处理麻烦而不把它弄得更糟。我在那儿待了三年。走的时候她送了我一本书。那本书我还留着，也还是读不下去。"},"jump":{"tw":[["rise",0],["shy",3],["change",2],["drop",6],["spring",0],["bounce",3],["enter",2],["climb",6],["start",0]],"en":"The rabbit would jump the low wall in one movement and drop into the field on the other side. My sister, who was shy, would start every time she saw it. In spring they came into the garden and would bounce around the young plants. I used to climb the wall and watch them until the light began to change. The number of them seemed to rise each year and then fall again. I never dared to enter that field. I was not a brave child. I would sit on the warm stones and count them out loud, one by one.","zh":"那只兔子一下就能跳过矮墙，落到另一边的地里。我妹妹胆子小，每回看见都要一惊。春天它们进园子，在新苗周围蹦来蹦去。我常爬上墙头看它们，一直看到天色变了。它们的数目一年年像是多起来，后来又少下去。我从没敢进那块地。我不是个胆大的孩子。我会坐在晒热的石头上，一个一个数出声来。"},"keep":{"tw":[["continue",3],["carry",3],["act",2],["break",1],["sure",6],["hold",3],["control",3],["cook",2],["save",0]],"en":"My grandmother had to keep the household going for thirty years, through the war and after it. She would cook three meals a day and carry the water from the well before sunrise. She had to hold her tongue when her husband acted badly, and she had to control her face in front of the children. She would save every scrap of paper. There was a break in her life that she never spoke about. She was sure of very few things, she said, but she was sure of the house. So she continued. The house is mine now, and it is still standing.","zh":"我奶奶得把这个家撑三十年，从战时一直到战后。她一天做三顿饭，天不亮就去井边挑水。丈夫做事不像样的时候，她得管住嘴；在孩子面前，她得管住自己的脸色。每一片纸她都留着。她这辈子有过一道坎，她从没提过。她说她能确定的事很少，但这座房子她是确定的。于是她就这么撑下来了。房子现在归我了，还立在那儿。"},"kick":{"tw":[["charge",0],["report",3],["blow",2],["minute",6],["bang",0],["protest",3],["dance",2],["ball",6],["beef",0]],"en":"A boy gave the gate a hard kick, and the bang brought the whole street to the window. He wanted to protest about something, but he could not say what. Then he took a ball and began to kick it against the wall, once a minute. A man came out and asked him to stop, and the boy answered him with a blow to the air. Later the shop reported the damage and did not charge us for it. At the village dance that night he was the first on the floor. He had eaten nothing but beef and bread.","zh":"一个男孩朝大门狠狠踢了一脚，那声巨响把整条街的人都叫到了窗前。他想抗议点什么，可自己也说不清。然后他拿了个球，一分钟往墙上踢一下。有人出来叫他停手，他朝空中挥了一下拳头算是回答。后来铺子报了损失，也没让我们赔。那天晚上村里的舞会上，头一个下场的就是他。他一整天只吃了牛肉和面包。"},"kid":{"tw":[["fry",0],["orphan",3],["tease",2],["boy",6],["minor",0],["peanut",3],["leather",2],["dude",6],["jolly",0]],"en":"The kid next door was an orphan, and he lived with an aunt who fried peanuts and sold them in paper bags. A bigger boy used to tease him about his leather shoes, which were too large and had belonged to someone else. He was a minor, so nobody could do much about it. But he was a jolly child, and he never once told on them. The young dude on the corner would buy a bag every day and say nothing. That small kindness was the whole of his luck. He is a tall man now, with a shop of his own.","zh":"隔壁那个小孩是个孤儿，跟一个姨妈过，姨妈炸花生米，用纸袋装着卖。有个大点的男孩总拿他那双皮鞋取笑他，那鞋太大，是别人穿过的。他还是未成年人，谁也不好插手。可他是个快活的孩子，一次也没告过状。街角那个年轻小子每天来买一袋，什么也不说。这点好意就是他的全部运气。现在他是个高个子了，自己开了家铺子。"},"kill":{"tw":[["pop",0],["shoot",3],["drink",2],["destroy",6],["defeat",0],["stone",3],["end",2],["escape",6],["obliterate",0]],"en":"The frost that year killed almost everything in the garden, and it was the end of my mother's roses. My father used to shoot the birds that came for the seed, though he never meant to kill them; he aimed above their heads. Then one dry summer a fire came up the hill and seemed to destroy the whole wood. We could hear a sharp pop from the trees. It was the only time I saw him drink in the daytime. He said the weather could defeat any man, and that a single stone of hail could obliterate a year of work. My mother escaped it all by sleeping.","zh":"那年的霜几乎把园子里的一切都冻死了，我母亲的玫瑰也就此完了。父亲以前会打那些来吃种子的鸟，不过他并不想打死它们，总是往头顶上打。后来有个干旱的夏天，火从山坡上烧上来，好像要把整片林子都毁了。我们能听见树里噼啪的响声。那是我唯一一次看见他白天喝酒。他说天能打垮任何人，一颗冰雹就能把一年的活计抹掉。我母亲一直睡着，什么也没赶上。"},"knock":{"tw":[["bang",0],["attack",3],["blow",2],["grab",6],["bump",0],["blame",3],["hit",2],["pull",6],["pink",0]],"en":"Someone gave a knock at the door at three in the morning, and then a second bang that woke the dog. My father pulled the bolt and opened it a little. A young woman stood there with a pink scarf over her head; her hand was bleeding and she could not say where the blow had come from. He did not blame her for anything. He told her to sit, then he grabbed a cloth and told me to bump the kettle onto the stove. Nobody had attacked anyone, as it turned out. She had simply hit the kerb with her bicycle.","zh":"凌晨三点有人敲门，接着又是一声重响，把狗都吵醒了。父亲拉开插销，把门开了一条缝。门外站着个年轻女人，头上搭着条粉色的围巾；她的手在流血，自己也说不清那一击是从哪儿来的。他一句也没有怪她，只叫她坐下，然后抓了块布，让我把水壶磕到炉子上去。后来才知道，谁也没袭击谁。她只是自行车撞到了路沿。"},"land":{"tw":[["bring",2],["floor",3],["arrive",2],["property",6],["country",0],["forest",3],["change",2],["territory",6],["earth",0]],"en":"The land my family bought was poor, a thin strip between the forest and the road. My father used to say that in this country a man who owns property owns trouble. He would bring back stones from the field and use them to build up the floor of the barn. When we arrived there in the spring, the whole place seemed about to change. Beyond the fence the territory belonged to somebody else, and we never crossed it. He turned the earth with his own hands for eleven years. The barn is a ruin now, and the forest has taken the rest.","zh":"我家买下的那块地很贫，是林子和大路之间窄窄一条。父亲常说，在这个国家，有地的人就有麻烦。他会从地里把石头捡回来，用来垫高谷仓的地面。我们春天到那儿的时候，整个地方都像是要变样了。篱笆那一边的地界是别人的，我们从没越过去。他用自己的手翻了十一年的土。谷仓现在塌了，剩下的地方被林子占了。"},"lead":{"tw":[["chair",3],["hand",3],["position",2],["deficit",1],["second",6],["head",0],["captain",3],["round",6],["leave",2]],"en":"The chair of the committee asked the captain to lead the discussion, and she took her position at the head of the table. There was a deficit in the accounts, and every round of talks ended in the same place. A man in the second row raised his hand and asked to speak. Nobody would second him, so he sat down again. The chair had to leave early for another meeting. Afterwards I asked her whether she would take the post again next year. She said she would, and that surprised me. She had been doing it for nine years by then.","zh":"委员会的主席请船长来主持这场讨论，她在长桌的主位坐了下来。账上有个缺口，每一轮谈来谈去都停在同一个地方。第二排一个人举手要求发言。没人附议他，他又坐下了。主席得先走，去赶另一个会。会后我问她，明年这个位子她还接不接。她说接，这让我有点意外。那时候她已经做了九年了。"},"leg":{"tw":[["stage",0],["pin",3],["cut",2],["thigh",6],["branch",0],["fork",3],["support",2],["knee",6],["peg",0]],"en":"His left leg had been bad since the accident, and the knee would not bend. He had to support himself on a stick cut from a branch at the fork of the old tree. There was a peg by the door where he hooked it at night. The wound on his thigh had healed but he still kept a pin in his coat. We walked the road in stages, and at each stage he would sit and rest. Nobody ever heard him complain. He used to say a leg is only a leg. He died at seventy, on a Sunday.","zh":"他的左腿从那次事故以后就一直不行，膝盖弯不下去。他得靠一根棍子撑着，那棍子是从老树分叉处砍下来的一根枝子。门边有个木钉，晚上他把棍子挂在那儿。大腿上的伤好了，可他外套口袋里还是揣着根别针。我们走那段路是分段的，每走一段他就坐下歇歇。从没听人听他抱怨过。他常说，一条腿就是一条腿。他七十岁那年走了，是个星期天。"},"lift":{"tw":[["raise",0],["climb",3],["better",2],["pull",6],["rise",3],["shoulder",3],["call",2],["push",6],["wind",0]],"en":"My father would lift the bag onto his shoulder without a word, then climb the stairs to the third floor. He had to pull himself up by the rail when the wind was strong at the door. There was no lift in that building, so every delivery was a slow rise from the street. He said the work made him better and not worse. Once he had to call a doctor for another man whose back had gone. We pushed the cart together after that. I was ten, and I could not raise the bag at all. He never asked me to try again.","zh":"父亲一句话不说就把麻袋扛上肩，然后爬上三楼。门口风大的时候，他得拽着栏杆把自己往上拉。那栋楼里没有电梯，所以每送一趟货都是从街上一层层慢慢上。他说这活儿让他身子变好了，不是变坏。有一次他还得替另一个背伤了的男人叫了大夫。从那以后我们一起推车。那年我十岁，那麻袋我根本举不动。他再没叫我试过。"},"list":{"tw":[["lean",2],["post",3],["move",2],["represent",6],["heel",0],["schedule",3],["position",2],["exception",6],["tilt",0]],"en":"The ship began to list to one side before we had left the harbour. The cargo had moved in the night, and the whole deck started to tilt. The mate would lean over the rail and shout the position of every post along the shore. Our schedule had to change, and for once nobody made an exception. My heel hurt for a week from standing so long. The captain sent a man to represent us at the port office. He said a list of that kind is not a small thing in open water. We reached the next port two days late.","zh":"船还没出港就开始往一侧倾。夜里的货挪了位，整层甲板都歪了起来。大副会趴在栏杆上喊出沿岸每一个标桩的位置。我们的日程只好改，这一回谁也没破例。我站得太久，脚后跟疼了一个星期。船长派了一个人去港务处代表我们。他说在大海上，这种倾斜可不是小事。我们晚了两天才到下一个港口。"},"listen":{"tw":[["hear",0],["attend",3],["concentrate",2],["tell",6],["mind",0],["incline",3],["obey",2],["speak",6],["heed",0]],"en":"My mother would listen at the door before she came into a room. She could hear what was not said, and she would not tell us what she thought. She had a mind of her own, and she did not always obey my father. In the evening she would incline her head towards the radio and concentrate on the news. We learned to speak quietly in that house. If you did not heed her one warning, you got no second one. She would not attend any meeting where people simply shouted. I have never met anyone who listened the way she did.","zh":"我母亲进任何一间屋之前，总先在门口听一听。她听得出没说出口的话，却从不把她的想法告诉我们。她有自己的主意，也不是什么都听我父亲的。傍晚她会把头偏向收音机，专心听新闻。在那栋房子里，我们都学会了低声说话。她的一句提醒你要是没听进去，就没有第二句。凡是只靠嚷嚷的会，她都不去。我从没见过谁像她那样听人说话。"},"load":{"tw":[["charge",0],["pack",3],["concern",2],["extra",6],["stretch",0],["pill",3],["fill",2],["handle",6],["burden",0]],"en":"The load on the cart was heavier than it looked, and the man had to pack it twice before it would hold. He would charge a small sum for the extra weight. His only concern was the horse, which had to stretch its neck to pull at all. He would fill a bag with food and take a pill for his back before they set out. The handle of the cart was smooth and dark. He said a burden shared is half a burden. Then he took the whole weight himself. I have never forgotten that cold morning, or the sound of the wheels.","zh":"车上的货比看上去重，那人装了两回才装住。多出来的分量他会收一点钱。他唯一惦记的是那匹马，它得伸长脖子才拉得动。出发前他会装一袋吃的，再吃一片治背的药。车把被磨得又滑又黑。他说，担子分着挑就轻一半。可最后整副重量还是他自己扛的。那个冷清的早晨，还有车轮的响声，我一直没忘。"},"look":{"tw":[["appear",0],["cut",3],["care",2],["how",6],["bet",0],["eye",3],["lie",2],["little",6],["count",0]],"en":"Take a good look at that photograph and tell me how many people you can count. My aunt had a look of her own, and she did not care what the neighbours thought of it. She would appear at the gate with her hair cut short and her eye on the weather. I would bet she never told a lie in her life. There was very little money in that house, and that was the one thing she minded. She said a face is only a face, and it does not decide anything. I still have her photograph on the wall.","zh":"好好看看那张照片，告诉我你能数出几个人。我姑妈有她自己的那副神情，邻居怎么看，她不在乎。她会站在大门口，头发剪得短短的，眼睛盯着天色。我敢打赌她一辈子没说过一句谎话。那家里没什么钱，这是她唯一放在心上的一件事。她说，脸就是一张脸，它决定不了什么。她的照片我还挂在墙上。"},"lord":{"tw":[["master",0],["count",3],["god",2],["lady",1],["sir",6],["divine",0],["peer",3],["king",6],["noble",0]],"en":"The old lord of that valley was a hard master, and nobody in the village would say so to his face. He was the count of three small towns, and he liked to be called sir. His lady came from a noble house and never once spoke to a servant. People said the king himself had given him the land as a reward. He would talk of divine right as if it were a fact. A peer from the next valley came once a year to hunt with him. They called each other friend. They did not mean it. At the harvest he thanked God and then raised the rent.","zh":"那一带的老爷是个厉害的主人，村里没人敢当着他的面这么说。他是三个小镇的伯爵，喜欢别人称他阁下。他的夫人出身贵族，从没跟下人说过一句话。人们说，这片地是国王亲自赏给他的。他谈起神授之权来，像是在说一件事实。邻谷的一位贵族每年过来一次，跟他一起打猎。他们互称朋友，可并不是。收庄稼的时候他谢过上帝，然后就把租子涨了。"},"lot":{"tw":[["deal",3],["party",3],["condition",2],["maybe",6],["draw",0],["flood",3],["divide",2],["good",6],["luck",0]],"en":"A lot of the fields by the river were under water that spring, and the flood took the lower road as well. The condition of the soil after it went down was not good. We had to divide what was left of the seed between three families by drawing straws, and our party drew the shortest one. Maybe that was the last piece of bad luck that year. My father made a deal with the mill and got us through. He said a man should not complain about the draw he is given. He put the seed in the ground and never spoke of it again.","zh":"那年春天河边很多地都泡在水里，洪水连下面那条路也冲了。水退之后土的情况不太好。剩下的种子要在三户人家之间分，我们用抽签的办法，我家抽到最短的一根。也许那就是那一年最后一件倒霉事。父亲跟磨坊谈成了一笔交易，把我们撑了过去。他说，抽到什么签，不该抱怨。他把种子埋进地里，这事以后再没提过。"},"engine":{"tw":[["engineer",4],["locomotive",0],["generator",3],["motor",2],["diesel",6],["catapult",3],["prototype",6]],"en":"In the shed by the station, an old engineer was working on the engine of a small locomotive. He had built the first prototype himself, years ago, and it still ran on diesel. A generator stood in the corner, humming beside the tools. The floor was dark with oil, and it smelled of hot metal. He had once tried to fit an electric motor into it, but the machine was too heavy. Above the door hung a strange catapult he had made as a boy. Outside, a train went by and shook the wall. He said the secret of any engine was patience, not power.","zh":"车站旁的棚屋里，一位老工程师正在修一台小机车的发动机。第一台样机是他多年前亲手造的，至今还烧柴油。角落里立着一台发电机，在工具旁边嗡嗡响。地板上油黑一片，满是热金属的味道。他曾试着给它装一个电动机，可这机器太重了。门上方挂着一个他小时候做的古怪投石机。外面有列火车经过，把墙都震动了。他说任何发动机的秘诀都是耐心，不是力气。"},"govern":{"tw":[["governance",4],["rule",0],["reign",3],["control",2],["mandate",6],["regulate",0],["unify",6]],"en":"For many years one old mayor governed our small island. His reign was long and quiet, and people trusted him. He knew every family by name, and every field. He believed good governance meant few new rules, and he would not regulate every little thing. He had a clear mandate from the voters, and he used it well. His aim was to unify the two villages, not to control them. He listened more than he spoke, and the water stayed clean. When he finally retired, the council had to govern without him. It took them a year to agree on anything.","zh":"很多年里，一位老镇长管理着我们这个小岛。他的任期又长又平静，人们信得过他。他叫得出每一户人家、每一块田的名字。他相信好的治理就是少立新规矩，不愿事事都去管。选民给了他清清楚楚的授权，他也用得妥当。他的目标是让两个村子合到一起，而不是去控制它们。他更多是听，不是讲，水质也一直干净。等他终于退下来，议事会就得在没有他的情况下治理这地方了。他们花了一年才在一件事上谈拢。"},"high":{"tw":[["highness",4],["overdrive",3],["degree",2],["low",1],["lower",6],["gear",2],["school",6]],"en":"We drove up into the hills, and the road climbed to a very high point before it turned. My uncle shifted into a lower gear and told me not to go into overdrive on the bends. The engine worked at a high degree of heat that day. Down in the valley we could see a low cloud over the school. From up here, everything looked small. He said that even his highness the mayor would have to slow down on a road like this. We laughed, and the car rolled on. The air was thin and cold. I wished the drive would never end.","zh":"我们开车往山里走，路一直爬到很高的地方才拐弯。我叔换了低挡，叫我在弯道上别用超速挡。那天发动机热得厉害。谷底那边，我们能看见一小片低云压在学校的上方。从这高处看下去，什么都变小了。他说，就连他那位市长大人，碰上这样的路也得慢下来。我们都笑了，车继续往前滚。空气又薄又冷。我真希望这趟车永远不要停。"},"idea":{"tw":[["ideal",4],["mind",0],["plan",3],["opinion",2],["theme",0],["impression",3],["purpose",2]],"en":"The whole idea came to me while I was walking home. In my mind I could already see the small shop, clean and warm. I asked my friend what she thought, and her opinion was the same as mine. The plan was simple: sell bread in the morning and close by noon. The theme of the place would be old and quiet, like a kitchen from long ago. I wanted to give people the impression that they had come home. That was the real purpose of it all. It was not an ideal plan, but it was ours.","zh":"这个主意是我走回家时想出来的。在我心里，那家小店已经清清楚楚：干净、暖和。我问朋友怎么想，她的看法和我一样。计划很简单：早上卖面包，中午就关门。这家店的调子要老派、安静，像很久以前的厨房。我想让人有种回到家似的感觉。这就是它真正的意义。这计划算不上多理想，可它是我们自己的。"},"inform":{"tw":[["informative",4],["report",3],["change",2],["advise",6],["tell",3],["communicate",2],["consult",6]],"en":"The manager called me in to inform me about a change in the schedule. He wanted me to consult the team before anything was decided. His report was short and clear, and he asked me to tell the others that morning. I had to communicate the news in a way that would not worry them. The talk was more informative than I had expected. He even asked me to advise him on the best day for the meeting. I wrote it down twice so I would not forget a single name. It felt good to be trusted with it. By noon everyone knew.","zh":"经理把我叫进去，通知我日程有变动。他希望在做决定之前，我先跟团队商量一下。他的报告简短清楚，让我当天上午就告诉大家。我得把这个消息传达出去，还不能让大伙儿担心。这次谈话比我预想的更有内容。他甚至让我就哪天开会最合适给他出主意。我写了两遍，生怕漏掉一个名字。被托付这件事，感觉挺好。到中午，所有人都知道了。"},"long":{"tw":[["longing",4],["yearn",0],["ache",3],["desire",2],["short",1],["once",6],["over",6]],"en":"She had been away for a long time, and a quiet longing had settled in her chest. She would yearn for the sound of rain on her old roof. There was an ache in her that no letter could ease. Her only desire was to go back, if only for a short visit. Once she had promised herself she would never return. Now, as the year moved over into spring, she began to think again. The road home was long, but she knew every turn. It was not far in miles, only in years. She left her bag by the door, ready.","zh":"她离家很久了，胸口慢慢积起一丝安静的思念。她会想念老屋顶上雨点的声音。她心里有块地方隐隐作痛，是信件治不好的。她唯一的愿望就是回去一趟，哪怕只住短短几天。她曾对自己发誓再也不回去了。如今，当一年跨进春天，她又开始动摇了。回家的路很长，可每一个拐弯她都认得。那不算多远，远的是那些年月。她把包放在门边，随时准备走。"},"employ":{"tw":[["use",0],["fill",3],["state",2],["involve",6],["apply",0],["play",3],["enable",6],["engage",0]],"en":"The old mill used to employ forty people, and now it takes only twelve. When the manager wants to fill a place, he asks people to apply at the gate, and he reads every form himself. The work does not involve much skill; you learn it in a week. A good worker will engage with the machine the way a player engages with a game. New tools enable one man to do what three once did. The state pays part of the wage in winter. I worked there one summer, and I used to watch the older men, who knew every sound the mill could make.","zh":"那家旧厂从前雇四十个人，如今只留十二个。经理想补一个缺，就让人们到大门口来应聘，每张表他都亲自看。这活儿不需要多少技术，一个星期就学会了。好工人跟机器打交道，就像玩家跟游戏打交道。新工具让一个人能干过去三个人的活。冬天国家替厂里付一部分工资。我在那儿干过一个夏天，常看那些老师傅，机器的每一声响他们都听得出来。"},"excite":{"tw":[["charge",0],["work",3],["disturb",2],["mystify",6],["shake",0],["disgust",3],["disappoint",6],["stir",0]],"en":"The new play did not excite the small audience the way the director had hoped. The first act seemed to mystify them, and the second began to disgust a few who had come for a comedy. Not even a sudden charge of drums could shake or disturb the calm in the room. One loud note did stir a boy in the front row, but most people only shifted in their seats. The director feared the ending would disappoint everyone. Yet when the lights went up, a few stood and clapped for the young woman who had done all the work. That alone was enough to excite him again.","zh":"这出新戏没能让小小的观众席兴奋起来，导演本指望它能。第一幕似乎把大家弄糊涂了，第二幕开始让几个想看喜剧的人觉得恶心。连一阵骤然响起的鼓点也没能搅动、惊扰屋里的那份安静。只有一声响让前排一个男孩动了动，其余人只是挪了挪身子。导演担心结局会让所有人失望。可灯亮起来时，还是有几个人站起来，为那个干了全部活儿的年轻女人鼓掌。单是这一点，就足够让他再兴奋一年。"},"eye":{"tw":[["centre",0],["seat",3],["hole",2],["ear",6],["heart",0],["look",2],["nose",6],["middle",0]],"en":"My grandfather had a seat in the centre of the old hall, and from there he could keep one eye on everything. He would look at the stage, then at the people around him, and say he could read a whole story from a face. A small hole in the ceiling let in a thin line of light, right over the middle of the room. He had a good ear for music and a warm heart for anyone who sang badly. Once, when a young woman tripped, he only touched his nose and smiled. Age had taken much from him, but not his eye.","zh":"我爷爷在旧礼堂正中有一个座位，从那儿他能用一只眼睛盯住所有动静。他会看看台上，再看看周围的人，说他能从一个脸上读出一整个故事。天花板上有个小洞，透下一道细细的光，正好落在屋子中央。他耳朵好，对唱得再糟的人也有一颗热心。有一次一个年轻女人绊了一下，他只是摸了摸鼻子，笑了笑。年纪带走了他很多东西，但没带走他这双眼睛。"},"fat":{"tw":[["fertile",0],["belly",3],["change",2],["thin",1],["milk",6],["plump",0],["lipid",2],["diet",6]],"en":"On my uncle's farm the land was fertile and the cows gave good milk, so nothing stayed thin for long. The oldest cow was plump, with a heavy belly, and the vet said her diet had too much fat in it. My uncle would change the feed each season and watch the animals grow. He liked a good layer of fat on a pig; it kept the meat soft. In the cold months the extra lipid under the skin kept them warm. He said a farm teaches you that fat is not always a fault.","zh":"我叔的农场土地肥沃，奶牛产的奶也好，所以什么都瘦不下来。最老的那头牛胖乎乎的，肚子很沉，兽医说它的饲料里脂肪太多。我叔每季换一次料，看着牲畜长起来。他喜欢猪身上有一层好膘，肉才软嫩。天冷的时候，皮底下那层多余的脂质能给它们保暖。他说农活会教你，肥不一定是毛病。"},"figure":{"tw":[["build",0],["allow",3],["body",2],["ground",1],["same",6],["enter",0],["imagine",2],["form",0]],"en":"The potter would build a small figure from a single lump of clay, first the body, then the arms, then the face. She could imagine the whole form before she touched it. The ground near her bench was always dusty, and she would allow no one to enter her workroom. Each piece took the same care, whether it was a bird or a queen. She said the number on the price card did not figure much in her mind; the shape did. She made nothing that was ever quite finished.","zh":"陶工会用一团泥捏出一个小人，先做身子，再做胳膊，再做脸。还没动手，她心里就已经有了整个形状。她工作台边的地上总是蒙着灰，她不许任何人进她的工作室。每一件都同样用心，不管是只鸟还是位女王。她说价签上的数字在她心里不算什么，形状才算。她做的东西从没有真正完工的。"},"finger":{"tw":[["feel",0],["index",3],["touch",2],["nose",6],["thumb",3],["indicate",2],["hand",6],["digit",2]],"en":"The old clockmaker would feel each little wheel with one finger before he set it in place. He never used his thumb for fine work; the index finger was the one he trusted. When a part was too small to see, he would bring his nose almost to the bench and let his touch tell him the truth. He could indicate a fault without a word, just by tapping the dial. Once he cut one hand and could not work for a week, and he said the smallest finger knew things the eye could not. To him every digit was a tool.","zh":"老钟表匠在装每一只小轮子之前，都要先用一根手指摸一摸。细活儿他从不用拇指，信得过的是那根食指。碰上小到看不清的零件，他会把鼻子凑到工作台前，靠手感辨出真相。他不用说话，敲敲表盘就能指出毛病。有一次他割破了一只手，一个星期干不了活，他说最小的那根手指知道眼睛不知道的事。对他来说每根指头都是工具。"},"flat":{"tw":[["straight",0],["box",2],["sharp",1],["above",6],["plane",0],["plain",2],["lower",6],["mat",0]],"en":"The workbench in the shed was flat and old, and my father kept it that way with a plane he had owned for years. He would lay a mat under each piece so it would not slip, and then draw a straight line along the edge. Above the bench hung a box of tools, and the lower shelf held the heavy ones. A sharp blade was the whole secret, he said. The plain wood would take a finish only if the surface was true. I learned to check with my palm, not my eye.","zh":"棚子里那张工作台又平又旧，我爸用一把用了多年的刨子把它一直保持这样。他会在每块木料下垫一张垫子，免得滑，再沿着边画一条直线。台子上方挂着一箱工具，下面那层架子放重的。他说秘诀全在一把快刃上。只有台面真正平整，素木才吃得住漆。我学会了用手掌去摸，而不是用眼睛看。"},"forget":{"tw":[["leave",0],["slip",3],["lose",2],["mind",1],["maybe",6],["block",0],["neglect",2],["imagine",6]],"en":"My grandfather began to forget small things first: where he had left his keys, the name of a street, the day of the week. He would lose his way in a town he had lived in all his life. Sometimes a word would slip away in the middle of a sentence, and he would laugh, though his mind was not laughing. The doctors said a small block in the brain could do this. He would neglect to eat, and we would have to remind him. Maybe, he said, it is better to imagine the past than to hold it.","zh":"爷爷是先从小事上开始忘的：钥匙搁哪儿了、一条街的名字、今天是星期几。他会在一座住了一辈子的镇上迷路。有时话说到一半，一个词就溜走了，他会笑，可他的脑子并没在笑。医生说脑里有一小块堵塞就能这样。他会忘了吃饭，我们得提醒他。他说，也许想象过去比抓住过去更好。"},"forward":{"tw":[["ahead",0],["position",2],["reverse",1],["goal",6],["forth",0],["transport",2],["right",6],["fore",0]],"en":"The boat moved forward with every pull, and the cox would call the time from the back. Our position in the race was third, then second, and we could see the leaders just ahead. The wind held us back, so the coach told us to lean forth and not to reverse our rhythm. On the right bank an old transport barge sat low in the water, and someone waved. Our only goal was the bridge. I could not feel my arms, but I kept pulling. Fore and aft the oars rose and fell together.","zh":"船随着每一次划桨向前走，舵手在后头喊节奏。我们在比赛里先是第三，然后第二，能看见前面的领头船就在不远处。风顶着我们，教练叫我们身体前倾、别乱了节奏。右岸停着一条笨重的运输驳船，有人在招手。我们唯一的目标就是那座桥。胳膊早就没了知觉，我还是一直划。船头船尾，桨一起升起，一起落下。"},"friend":{"tw":[["champion",0],["companion",3],["advocate",2],["foe",1],["father",6],["ally",0],["confederate",3],["wife",6]],"en":"My father was a quiet man, but in a fight he was a true friend. When a neighbour was accused of stealing, he stood up as her champion and spoke for her like an advocate in a court. Her only companion in that room was him. The rest had turned into a foe overnight. He called in an old ally from the next village, a man some people thought a confederate of thieves, and together they found the missing receipt. My mother, his wife, said nothing until they came home. Then she smiled and put the kettle on.","zh":"我爸是个安静的人，可真到较劲的时候，他是个够格的朋友。有个邻居被指偷东西，他站出来替她当靠山，像法庭上的辩护人一样为她说话。那屋里，她唯一的同伴就是他。其余的人一夜之间都成了对头。他请来邻村一个老盟友，有人说那人是贼的同伙，两人一起找出了那张丢失的收据。我妈，也就是他妻子，一直到他们回家都没作声。然后她笑了，把水壶放上炉子。"},"full":{"tw":[["good",0],["beat",2],["empty",1],["same",6],["total",0],["change",2],["own",6],["wide",0]],"en":"The hall was full an hour before the film began, and the queue outside was wide and noisy. A good film, the manager said, always beat a bad one on the first night, and this one was both. The room had been empty all week, and now every seat was taken. The same thing happened every winter, and each time he would change the posters by the door. He would say the total had doubled over the year. His own small office was behind the screen. When the lights went down, nobody spoke.","zh":"电影开场前一小时，放映厅就坐满了，外头排的队又宽又吵。经理说，头一晚好片子总能压过烂片子，而这一部两者都占。整整一周厅里都空着，现在每个位子都有人。每年冬天都是这样，每回他都会换掉门口的海报。他会说这一年的总数翻了一倍。他自己的小办公室就在银幕后面。灯一暗，谁都不说话了。"},"further":{"tw":[["advance",0],["carry",3],["support",2],["result",6],["encourage",0],["feed",3],["due",6],["boost",0]],"en":"The teacher said we needed further tests before we could trust the result. She would encourage us to advance one step at a time, and to carry our notes to every lesson. The school gave small support for materials, nothing more. We had to feed the plants by hand each morning and write down every change. A boost of light made one row grow faster, but that was due to the weather, not to our plan. When the first numbers came in better than we hoped, we could not stop talking about it.","zh":"老师说，在相信这个结果之前，我们还需要做进一步的试验。她会鼓励我们一步一步推进，把笔记带到每一节课上。学校给的材料费很少，就这么点支持。我们得每天早上亲手给植物喂水，记下每一点变化。多一点光照让一排长得更快，可那是天气的缘故，不是我们的方案。当第一批数据比我们希望的还好时，我们聊得停不下来。"},"glass":{"tw":[["ice",0],["goblet",3],["change",2],["plastic",6],["chalk",0],["mirror",2],["metal",6],["glaze",0]],"en":"The glassblower would take a long metal pipe and draw a ball of hot glass from the fire. He would change the shape for every customer, and the fire decided how far he could go. A goblet was the hardest thing to make, because the rim had to be thin and even. It was nothing like a plastic cup, he said; glass has a memory. He would draw a chalk line on the bench to mark each size. A pale blue glaze, like ice on a window, was his favourite finish, and when it was done it would shine like a mirror.","zh":"吹玻璃的人会拿一根长长的金属管，从火里带出一团滚烫的玻璃。他会为一个客人换一个形状，火决定他能走多远。高脚杯是最难做的，因为杯口又薄又匀。他说这跟塑料杯完全是两回事，玻璃是有记性的。他会用粉笔在案子上画线，标出每个尺寸。一层淡蓝的釉，像窗上的冰，是他最喜欢的收尾，做成之后会亮得像面镜子。"},"guess":{"tw":[["imagine",0],["tell",3],["calculate",2],["maybe",6],["judge",0],["estimate",2],["else",6],["suppose",0]],"en":"At the village fair there was a contest to guess the weight of a huge pumpkin. You could not calculate it exactly, so everyone had to estimate, and most people were far out. A farmer would judge each answer with a serious face and then tell them how close they were. Somebody asked if there was anything else to win, and the answer was no. I suppose the whole thing was silly, but it was fun. Maybe the winner simply had luck. I could imagine a hundred pumpkins of that size in one field, and not one of them easy. My own guess was four kilos wrong.","zh":"村子的集市上有个比谁猜得准的节目，猜一个大南瓜有多重。你没法精确算出来，只能估，多数人都差得离谱。一个农夫会一本正经地评判每个答案，然后告诉他们猜得有多近。有人问还有别的什么可赢吗，回答是没有。我想这事挺傻，可也真有意思。也许赢的人就是运气好。我能想象一整片地里长着一百个这么大的南瓜，而且一个都不好估。我自己的答案差了四公斤。"},"guy":{"tw":[["cat",0],["tease",3],["man",2],["pretty",6],["rib",0],["mock",2],["good",6],["roast",0]],"en":"The guy who lived next door was a good cook, and every summer he would roast a whole fish on the fire in his garden. His cat would sit on the wall and watch, one eye on the plate. He liked to tease his friends and would mock them gently, but he never meant harm. A rib or two about my old car was the price of dinner. He was a small, pretty quiet man until you knew him. One evening he told us how his father had taught him to cook. No one laughed then, and it turned into a very fine night.","zh":"隔壁那家伙是个好厨子，每年夏天都会在花园的火上烤一整条鱼。他的猫蹲在墙上看着，一只眼睛盯着盘子。他爱逗朋友，会轻轻地挖苦几句，可绝没有恶意。拿我那辆旧车开一两个玩笑，就是这顿饭的价钱。他不熟的时候是个安静的小个子，熟了才知道他多有意思。有天晚上他讲起他父亲是怎么教他做饭的。那会儿没人笑，一夜就这么过得很舒心。"},"have":{"tw":[["accept",3],["bring",3],["change",2],["lack",1],["already",6],["bear",3],["carry",3],["cause",0]],"en":"My aunt did not have much, but she would never accept help from anyone. Every week she would bring bread to the old woman upstairs and carry her shopping up the stairs. She said a lack of money was no cause for shame, and she could bear any amount of it. Things changed slowly in that building. She was already old herself, and her back hurt, but she kept going. She would sit with the woman and have tea, and neither of them said much. That small kindness was the only thing she could give, and she gave it.","zh":"我姑妈没什么钱，可她从不接受任何人的帮助。每个星期她都会给楼上的老太太送面包，帮她把买的东西搬上楼。她说缺钱不丢人，多少她都受得住。那栋楼里的事变得很慢。她自己年纪也大了，背又疼，可她还是照做。她会坐下来跟老太太喝杯茶，两个人都不怎么说话。那份小小的善意是她唯一能给的东西，她就这么给了。"},"history":{"tw":[["story",0],["annals",3],["past",2],["life",6],["account",0],["record",2],["literature",6],["chronicle",0]],"en":"My grandfather spent his last years writing the history of our family. He kept every account in a thick book, and he would read the old annals of the town to fill the gaps. The past, he said, is not one story but a hundred. He had lived a long life in one valley and could record the name of every field. He told us about a chronicle his own father had kept, and about the literature of the village fair. When he finished, he gave the book to me.","zh":"爷爷最后那几年一直在写我们家的历史。他把每一笔都用一本厚本子记下来，还会翻镇上的旧年鉴补上空白。他说过去不是一段故事，而是一百段。他在一个山谷里活了一辈子，能报出每一块地的名字。他跟我们讲过他父亲留下的一部编年记，还有村里集市上的那些文字。写完以后，他把本子交给了我。"},"horse":{"tw":[["buck",0],["hack",3],["provide",2],["dog",6],["knight",0],["pony",3],["cat",6],["cavalry",0]],"en":"At the riding school there was an old horse who would buck whenever a beginner took the reins. My sister, who was small, was given a pony instead, and she loved it. The school would provide a hat and a stick for every child. A dog and a cat lived in the yard and followed the riders about. On the wall hung a picture of a knight on horseback, and beside it a photo of the cavalry from a war long ago. I would hack out along the lane on Sundays, happy and slow.","zh":"马术学校里有一匹老马，哪个新手一拉缰绳它就尥蹶子。我妹妹个子小，被分到一匹小马驹，她喜欢得不得了。学校会给每个孩子发一顶帽子和一根鞭子。院子里还养着一条狗一只猫，跟着骑手转。墙上挂着一幅画，画的是骑在马上的骑士，旁边是一张很久以前那场战争里骑兵的照片。星期天我会骑着马慢慢溜达到小路那头，又自在又悠闲。"},"house":{"tw":[["family",2],["chamber",3],["play",2],["senate",6],["home",3],["lodge",3],["room",6],["sign",0]],"en":"The old house at the end of the lane had once been a public building. Long ago a small senate or council had met in its largest chamber, and men would stand and play at politics for hours. Later it became a family home, and each room held children. My grandfather lived there last, alone. He kept the old sign above the door, a wooden board with the town name on it. In winter the lodge at the back was the warmest place. When he died we sold the house, and I have not been inside since.","zh":"巷子尽头那座老屋以前是公家的地方。很久以前，一个小型元老会或议事会曾在它最大的厅里开过会，男人们一站就是几个钟头，拿政治当游戏。后来它成了一户人家的宅子，每个房间都住着孩子。最后是我爷爷一个人住在那儿。他把那块写着镇名的木牌留在了门楣上。冬天，屋后的门房是最暖和的地方。他去世后我们把房子卖了，我再没进去过。"},"hurt":{"tw":[["pain",0],["burn",3],["upset",2],["worse",6],["damage",2],["catch",3],["trouble",6],["harm",0]],"en":"My brother had a bad hurt after he fell from the ladder onto the stone floor. The pain was worst in his back, and the doctor said the damage could be worse than it looked. He had also caught a burn on his arm from the lamp. For a week he could not move without trouble, and the least noise would upset him. My mother said there was no harm in asking for help, but he would not. He sat by the window and watched the field. It took a whole spring before he could lift a box again, and he was never quite the same.","zh":"我哥从梯子上摔到石板地上，伤得不轻。最疼的是背，医生说损伤可能比看上去更重。他胳膊上还被灯燎出一块烫伤。有一个星期，他一动就麻烦，最轻的响动都会让他心烦。我妈说开口求人不丢人，可他就是不肯。他坐在窗边望着地里。整整一个春天过去，他才能再抬起一只箱子，而他也再没完全恢复成原来的样子。"},"joke":{"tw":[["laugh",0],["pun",3],["act",2],["stuff",6],["trick",0],["communicate",2],["fun",6],["gag",3]],"en":"My uncle could never tell a joke straight. He would act out every part, put on a voice, and add a terrible pun at the end. Half the fun was watching him try. The best gag he knew was about a man who lost his hat, and he told it every year. We would laugh until our sides hurt, though we had heard it all before. He said all that stuff about timing was mostly luck. His real trick was to keep people waiting for the last word. He could communicate more in one silly minute than most people manage in an hour.","zh":"我叔讲笑话从来讲不直。他会把每个角色都演一遍，换着嗓子，末了再塞一个糟糕的双关。一半的乐趣就在于看他怎么讲。他最拿手的一个段子讲的是一个人把帽子丢了，他每年都讲。我们笑得肚子疼，尽管早就听过。他说那些关于火候的话多半是碰运气。他真正的诀窍是让人等着最后一句。他一分钟傻话能传达的东西，比大多数人一个钟头还多。"},"kind":{"tw":[["form",0],["like",3],["category",2],["mind",6],["variety",0],["brand",3],["little",6],["genial",0]],"en":"The little shop on the corner sold every kind of tea you could name. The owner, a genial old man, would open a box and let you smell each one before you chose. There was a wide variety in a single shelf, and each brand had its own form and colour. He would ask what you had in mind and then point to a category you had never tried. I like the smoky ones best. He never rushed a customer, and he never sold the same leaf twice. I went there for years, and I still miss it.","zh":"街角那家小店卖你想得出的每一种茶。老板是个和气的老头，会打开盒子让你先闻一闻再挑。一层架子上就有很多花样，每个牌子都有自己的形状和颜色。他会问你想找什么，然后指给你一个你从没试过的品类。我最喜欢那些带烟熏味的。他从不催客人，也从不把同一批叶子卖两次。我在那儿买了好些年，到现在还惦记着。"},"lady":{"tw":[["madam",0],["duchess",3],["woman",2],["lord",1],["queen",6],["dame",0],["countess",3],["daughter",6]],"en":"In the great hall there hung a portrait of a lady in a dark dress, and the guide said she had been a duchess before she married. Beside her stood her lord, stiff and proud. Her daughter, a countess, was painted in the next room, and a queen looked down from the wall above the stairs. The old dame who kept the house would call every visitor madam, even the children. She was a small woman with a loud, kind voice. She said the family had lost its money long ago, and now only the house was left. I bought a postcard and walked home slowly.","zh":"大厅里挂着一幅画像，画中那位女士穿着深色长裙，导游说她出嫁前是一位公爵夫人。她身旁站着她丈夫，也就是那位老爷，身子挺拔，一脸傲气。隔壁房间画着她女儿，一位伯爵夫人；楼梯上方的墙上还有一位王后俯视着来客。看守这座宅子的老太太管每位游客都叫夫人，连孩子也不例外。她是个嗓门响亮、心地和善的小个子女人。她说这家人的钱早就败光了，如今只剩这座房子。我买了张明信片，慢慢走回了家。"},"laugh":{"tw":[["joke",0],["roar",3],["cry",1],["loud",6],["laughter",0],["chuckle",3],["fun",6],["gag",0]],"en":"The comedian opened with a joke so old that the whole room began to roar before he finished it. A loud man at the back gave a great cry of delight, and even the quiet ones had a chuckle. His best gag was about a broken boat, and it never failed. For an hour there was nothing but laughter in the small hall. I had not had so much fun in months. When he left the stage, his face was wet and his voice was gone. We walked home under the street lights, still laughing at the last line.","zh":"那位喜剧演员一上来讲了个老掉牙的笑话，还没讲完满屋子就哄然大笑。后排一个嗓门很大的男人痛快地喊了一嗓子，连安静的人也都轻声笑了。他最拿手的一个段子讲的是一条破船，从没失手过。整整一个钟头，小礼堂里除了笑声什么都没有。我好几个月没这么开心过。他下台的时候，满脸是汗，嗓子也哑了。我们走在路灯下往家走，还在为最后一句笑个不停。"},"lip":{"tw":[["mouth",0],["collar",3],["edge",2],["tongue",6],["rim",0],["margin",2],["ear",6],["brim",0]],"en":"The cold wind made her lip dry before we had gone a hundred steps. She pulled her collar up to her mouth and said nothing. Snow lay along the edge of the road, and the brim of her old hat was white with it. I could not feel my ears. At home she poured tea to the very rim of the cup, and a thin margin of the table stayed dry. She burned her tongue on the first sip and laughed. We sat by the window and watched the snow fill the garden, warm at last. It seemed the whole street had gone quiet.","zh":"还没走出一百步，冷风就把她的嘴唇吹干了。她把衣领拉到嘴边，一言不发。路边积着雪，她那顶旧帽子的帽檐上也白了一层。我的耳朵早没了知觉。回到家，她把茶倒到杯口那么满，桌面上只留一条窄窄的干边。第一口她就烫到了舌头，笑了一声。我们坐在窗边，看雪一点点把园子填满，身上终于暖了。整条街好像都静了下来。"},"lose":{"tw":[["miss",0],["drop",3],["regress",2],["find",1],["chance",6],["suffer",2],["forget",3],["enough",6]],"en":"When the new road opened, the small shop began to lose its customers. The owner would drop his prices again and again, but nothing helped. He did not want to regress to selling only bread, yet he had to. There was one last chance: a market day in spring. He could not forget the first year, when people had come from miles away, and he knew he would miss the bell over the door most of all. There was not enough money to pay the rent. He began to suffer in silence, and would not speak of it to anyone. In the end his son found him a job in the city, and the shop closed.","zh":"新路一通车，那家小店就开始流失客人。老板一遍遍地降价，可什么用都没有。他不想倒退到只卖面包的地步，可也只能这样。最后还有一个机会：春天的一场集市。他忘不了头一年，那时人们从几里外赶来；他也知道，他最想念的是门上那声铃响。钱不够付房租。他开始一个人默默受着，对谁都不提。最后他儿子替他在城里找了份活，店也关了。"},"low":{"tw":[["blue",0],["gear",2],["high",1],["less",6],["first",0],["utter",2],["rate",6],["small",0]],"en":"The old truck could not climb the hill in high gear, so the driver would shift down low and let it crawl. The rate of fuel in the tank was falling fast, and he had less than he needed. His first worry was the steep bend ahead. The motor gave a low, blue cloud of smoke, and he would utter a short word under his breath. A small car waited behind him, patient and slow. At the top he stopped and let the engine rest. The whole valley lay below, and the sky was clear.","zh":"那辆旧卡车挂高档爬不上坡，司机只好换到低档，让它慢慢往上蹭。油箱里的油掉得很快，他手里的比需要的还少。他头一个担心的就是前面那道陡弯。发动机吐出一团低低的、发蓝的烟，他压着嗓子嘟囔了一句。后面一辆小车耐心地跟着，开得很慢。到了坡顶他停下，让发动机歇一歇。整个山谷铺在脚下，天也晴了。"},"machine":{"tw":[["car",0],["wheel",3],["shape",2],["automatic",6],["automobile",0],["lever",3],["produce",2],["equipment",6]],"en":"The new machine in the factory could do the work of six men. It would pull a long strip of steel through two wheels and shape it into a door. A worker would push a lever, and the rest was automatic. The whole plant had once made cars, and an old automobile stood in the yard as a sign of that time. Now the equipment produced parts for other factories. My father said the machine never got tired and never asked for more pay. He liked it and feared it at the same time. In winter the hall was cold, but the machine stayed warm.","zh":"厂里这台新机器能顶六个人的活。它把一条长长的钢带从两个轮子中间拉过去，压成门的形状。工人推一下手柄，剩下的全是自动的。这家厂从前造过汽车，院子里摆着一辆旧汽车，算是那个年头的标记。如今这些设备给别的厂子生产零件。我爸说，机器从不累，也从不多要工钱。他一边喜欢它，一边又怕它。冬天厂房里很冷，可机器是热的。"},"egg":{"tw":[["ball",0],["spawn",3],["coat",2],["butter",6],["roe",3],["pelt",2],["milk",6]],"en":"Every spring the fish swim up the river to spawn, and their roe lies in the shallow water like small orange balls. My uncle would catch a few, clean them, and cook them with butter and milk. The skin he left on made a thin coat that kept them soft. The wind was cold and would pelt the window with rain. We ate the eggs with bread and said nothing. Later the river would be full of fish again. On the way home my uncle told me how the young ones would come back, years later, to the same water.","zh":"每年春天鱼都游上河来产卵，鱼卵像一颗颗小橙球躺在浅水里。我叔会捞上几条，收拾干净，用黄油和牛奶煎。他留着的那层皮形成薄薄一层衣，让鱼肉保持嫩。风很冷，夹着雨点打在窗上。我们就着面包吃鱼卵，谁也没说话。以后河里又会满是鱼。回家的路上，叔叔告诉我，那些小鱼多年后还会回到同一片水里。"},"exact":{"tw":[["claim",2],["call",3],["proof",6],["demand",0],["command",3],["specific",6],["accurate",0]],"en":"The manager wanted an exact number before he would sign anything. He did not accept my claim without proof, and he would not take a rough guess. His demand was specific: give me the accurate figure by noon. Then he picked up the phone to call the office and gave a short command to the clerk. I went back to my desk and counted everything twice. When I returned, he read the page slowly and nodded. I had never worked so carefully in my life. That evening I checked the same list three more times before I left.","zh":"经理在签字之前要一个精确的数字。没有证据，他就不接受我的说法，也不肯听个大概的估计。他的要求很明确：中午前把准确的数目给我。然后他拿起电话打给办公室，简短地吩咐了那位职员一句。我回到座位上，把每样东西数了两遍。回来时，他慢慢看完那页纸，点了点头。我这辈子从没这么仔细地做过事。那天晚上，我走之前又把同一张单子核了三遍。"},"fair":{"tw":[["clean",5],["join",2],["foul",1],["opportunity",6],["average",0],["appeal",6],["carnival",0]],"en":"The fair came to the field behind the school, and the whole town seemed to join in. There was a small carnival with lights, and an average crowd for a warm evening. My sister said the prices were not fair. We bought a clean white hat and watched the games. One player made a foul, and the crowd shouted. It was a good opportunity for the children, and the appeal of the music kept us there until dark. We walked home slowly, and she held my arm all the way.","zh":"集市来到学校后面的空地上，全镇的人好像都来凑热闹了。有个亮着灯的小游乐园，就一个暖和的傍晚来说，人算一般。我妹妹说价钱不公平。我们买了一顶干净的白帽子，看人玩那些游戏。有个玩家犯了规，人群就喊起来。对孩子们来说这是个好机会，音乐好听，把我们留到天黑。我们慢慢走回家，她一路挽着我的胳膊。"},"fast":{"tw":[["quick",5],["diet",3],["slow",1],["pace",6],["tight",0],["better",6],["firm",0]],"en":"My cousin could run fast, but he was on a diet that left him weak. He kept a slow pace at first, then a quick one, his shoes tight on the track. He said it was better to finish firm than to start strong. I watched him from the gate with a bottle of water. When he passed me, his face was calm and set. He did not stop until the light went down behind the hill. Later I asked him why he trained so hard, and he only smiled. He said a slow start had almost kept him from the race.","zh":"我表哥能跑得很快，却因在节食而没力气。他起初慢慢跑，随后加快，鞋子紧紧贴着跑道。他说，稳稳跑完比一开始冲得猛要好。我提着水瓶在门口看他。他经过我身边时，脸平静而绷着。他一直跑到山那头的光暗下去才停。后来我问他为什么练得这么狠，他只是笑。他说，起步太慢差点让他连比赛都赶不上。"},"fine":{"tw":[["ok",0],["book",2],["coarse",1],["well",6],["ticket",0],["penalty",2],["good",6]],"en":"The library sent me a fine for a book I had kept too long. The ticket said the penalty would grow each week. I told the woman at the desk that it was not ok, that I had been ill. She was good about it and said I could pay half. The paper of the old book felt coarse under my thumb. I said I was well enough now, and I wrote my name on the form. She smiled and wished me a fine weekend. I paid and left, and on the steps I promised never to keep a book so long again.","zh":"图书馆因为我超期留了一本书，给我寄来一张罚款单。单子上说罚金每周都会涨。我跟柜台的女士说这不行，我生病了。她很好说话，说我可以只付一半。那本旧书的纸摸上去粗粗的。我说我现在身体好了，在表格上写下名字。她笑笑，祝我周末愉快。我交了钱就走，在台阶上暗暗发誓再也不把书留这么久了。"},"fish":{"tw":[["angle",3],["rail",3],["catch",2],["meat",6],["salmon",3],["search",2],["shrimp",6]],"en":"We would fish from the old rail on the pier, my father and I, and search the water for any sign of movement. He taught me to angle the line so the bait would sink slowly. That day we did not catch a salmon, only a few shrimp and one small fish. He said the meat of the salmon was worth the wait. We stayed until the light failed, with our backs to the cold wind. On the walk home he talked about his own father, and the boats they had used before I was born.","zh":"我和父亲常在码头的旧栏杆边钓鱼，盯着水面找任何动静。他教我把钓线斜着放，好让饵慢慢下沉。那天我们没钓到鲑鱼，只有几只虾和一条小鱼。他说鲑鱼的肉值得等。我们一直待到天光暗下去，背对着冷风。回家的路上，他讲起他自己的父亲，还有我出生前他们用过的那些船。"},"forest":{"tw":[["wood",0],["jungle",3],["land",2],["pine",6],["timber",0],["plant",2],["swamp",6]],"en":"Behind the house the forest began and ran for miles. The wood was old, mostly pine and dark timber, and in the wet months part of it turned into swamp. My father would plant small trees along the edge each spring, and he knew every path on the land. Once we walked to the far side, where the trees grew so close they made a kind of jungle. He said a forest like this could not be bought with money, only kept. That was the last summer we walked it together.","zh":"房子后面就是森林，一直绵延好几英里。林木很老了，多半是松树和深色的成材木，到了潮湿的月份，有一部分会变成沼泽。每年春天我父亲都沿着边栽些小树，地里的每条路他都认得。有一回我们走到最远的那头，树挨得那么密，简直成了一片丛林。他说这样的森林花钱买不来，只能守着。那是我和他最后一次一起走过它。"},"general":{"tw":[["cosmopolitan",0],["head",2],["local",1],["chief",6],["ecumenical",0],["command",2],["secretary",6]],"en":"At the head of the table sat a retired general with a cosmopolitan manner. He had once held command of a large camp and had a local chief beside him. His secretary took notes in a small book. He spoke of the world with an ecumenical spirit, as if every town were his own. I was young and said little. When he shook my hand, he asked where I came from and listened to the answer as if it mattered. Years later I read his name in an old report, and I remembered that quiet evening.","zh":"长桌首端坐着一位退役将军，举止带着见过世面的气度。他曾经统辖一座大营，身边坐着当地的头人。他的秘书拿着小本子记东西。他谈起世界时怀着一视同仁的心，仿佛哪座城镇都是他的。我那时年轻，话不多。他握我的手时，问我是哪里人，听得很认真，仿佛这很重要。多年后我在一份旧报告里看到他的名字，又想起那个安静的傍晚。"},"girl":{"tw":[["daughter",0],["maid",3],["woman",2],["boy",1],["kid",6],["lass",3],["female",2]],"en":"Next door lived a girl of about ten, the daughter of the woman who kept the shop. She helped like a maid, carrying boxes and sweeping the step, and every boy and kid on the street liked her. Her mother called her a lass and told her to be careful. She was the only female in a house of four brothers and did not seem to mind. I watched her one afternoon, laughing at the gate. She grew up, left the town, and I never saw her again. But I still remember the way she carried those boxes without ever asking for help.","zh":"隔壁住着个十来岁的女孩，是开小店那女人的女儿。她像个帮工似的干活，搬箱子、扫台阶，街上每个男孩和小孩都喜欢她。她妈叫她丫头，叮嘱她小心点。家里四个兄弟，就她一个女孩，她好像也不在意。有天下午我在门口看着她笑。她长大了，离开了镇子，我再没见过她。可我至今记得她搬那些箱子的样子，从不开口求人。"},"glance":{"tw":[["glimpse",0],["hit",2],["preview",6],["glint",0],["look",2],["stumble",6],["peek",0]],"en":"I caught a glance of the letter as she turned, only a glimpse before she closed the drawer. There was a glint of gold at the edge of the paper. I tried not to peek, but I took one more look. Later I stumbled on the same box in the hall, and it hit my foot. She never said a word about it. Years afterward she showed me a preview of the old pages and smiled. It was a letter from my father, written the year before he died. I read it twice and put it back where I had found it.","zh":"她转身时，我瞥见了那封信，只一眼，抽屉就关上了。纸边有一点金光一闪。我本想不去偷看，可还是多看了一眼。后来我在过道里被同一只箱子绊了一下，撞到了脚。她从没提过这事。多年以后，她让我先看了那些旧信的一小部分，微微笑着。那是我父亲写的信，写在他去世前一年。我读了两遍，又放回原处。"},"god":{"tw":[["idol",0],["superior",2],["divine",6],["divinity",0],["effigy",2],["heaven",6],["deity",0]],"en":"In the old church the people prayed to a god they called the divine one. On the wall hung a small idol, an effigy of some ancient deity, and the light made it look almost alive. My grandmother said she did not need a statue to reach heaven. She spoke of divinity as something you could feel in your hands. Her superior in the order agreed with her. I sat at the back and listened. She was the only person in that room who never seemed afraid. When the candles went out, she took my hand and led me into the cold street without a word.","zh":"在那座老教堂里，人们向一位他们称为圣者的神祈祷。墙上挂着一尊小神像，是某位古神的塑像，灯光下看上去几乎活了。我奶奶说她不需要雕像也能上天堂。她说神性是一种你用手就能感觉到的东西。她在教会里的上司也同意她。我坐在后排听着。满屋子人里，只有她从不显得害怕。蜡烛灭时，她牵着我的手，一句话不说就带我走进寒冷的街上。"},"group":{"tw":[["radical",0],["race",3],["meet",2],["member",6],["team",3],["unit",2],["joint",6]],"en":"A small group of us would meet every Thursday in the back room. Each member belonged to a different club and had a different idea of the race ahead. One man held more radical views than the rest. We worked as one team, and in time we became a single unit. The joint project was small but ours. I still keep the list of names from those years. We lost touch after the work ended, but once a year one of them writes to me. He always asks about the others, and I never know what to say.","zh":"我们一小群人每个星期四在后屋碰头。每个人属于不同的俱乐部，对前面的那场角逐各有各的看法。有个人的想法比别人激进得多。我们像一个队那样干活，慢慢地成了一个整体。共同的项目不大，却是我们自己的。那些年的名单我还留着。活干完后大家便断了来往，可每年总有一个人给我写信，每次都问起其余的人，而我总不知该怎么答。"},"hate":{"tw":[["hatred",0],["abhor",3],["dislike",2],["love",1],["shame",6],["detest",0],["fear",6]],"en":"I did not hate the man who took my place; I only disliked him at first. My mother said hatred eats the one who holds it, and that fear does more harm than anger. I learned to abhor cruelty, and in time to detest any kind of lie. But I could not love him either, and that was my shame. We shook hands years later, in the street, and said nothing of the past. He was old by then, and thinner than I remembered. I walked home slowly and felt lighter than I had in years.","zh":"我并不恨那个顶了我位子的人，起初只是不喜欢他。我妈说，恨会啃噬怀着恨的人，而恐惧比愤怒伤害更大。我学会了憎恶残忍，后来也厌恶任何谎言。可我也没法喜欢他，这就是我的羞愧之处。多年后我们在街上握了手，谁都没提过去。那时他老了，比我记忆中瘦。我慢慢走回家，觉得多年没这么轻松过。"},"heavy":{"tw":[["big",5],["character",2],["light",1],["ground",6],["great",0],["fire",6],["hard",0]],"en":"The box was heavy, too big for me to carry alone. It held a great many books, and the ground was soft from the rain. My uncle had a hard, quiet character and would not complain. He took one end and I took the other, and we set it by the fire. The work was light compared with the farm, he said. We sat down and drank tea in the warmth. When I left that evening, he walked me to the gate and told me to come back with better shoes.","zh":"那口箱子很沉，大得我一个人搬不动。里面装了很多书，地上被雨泡软了。我叔性子又硬又静，从不抱怨。他抬一头，我抬一头，把箱子放到火边。他说，跟农场里的活比，这算轻的。我们坐下，在暖意里喝茶。那天傍晚我走时，他送我到门口，叫我下次来换双好鞋。"},"hell":{"tw":[["pit",0],["trouble",2],["heaven",1],["crazy",6],["sin",0],["cry",6],["blaze",0]],"en":"The summer was so hot it felt like hell. The old factory was a pit of dust, and the blaze of the furnaces never went out. The men said the heat would drive them crazy. My father called the long shifts a kind of trouble he could not leave. Someone began to cry near the gate. He told me that heaven and sin were far away compared with a day like this, and told me to go home. I walked the long road back and counted the windows that still had light. There were not many.","zh":"那年夏天热得像地狱。老厂是个满是灰尘的坑，炉火的烈焰从不熄灭。工人们说这热会把人逼疯。我父亲把这些长班叫做一种他离不开的苦。门口有人哭起来。他对我说，比起这样的一个白天，天堂和罪都远得很，然后叫我回家。我沿着长路往回走，数那些还亮着灯的窗户。没几扇。"},"ice":{"tw":[["glass",0],["cool",2],["hot",6],["frost",3],["cover",2],["dust",6],["chalk",0]],"en":"The pond had a cover of ice, thin as glass. In the frost the reeds looked white as chalk, and a little dust of snow lay on the bank. I put my hand on the cold surface; it was cool at first, then so cold it burned like hot iron. My sister drew lines with a stick. We heard the ice crack once, far out, and stepped back together. She asked if we could walk across it, and I said no. We went home the long way, along the road.","zh":"池塘上覆着一层冰，薄得像玻璃。霜里芦苇白得像粉笔，岸上落着一点雪末。我把手按在冰冷的表面上，起初是凉的，接着冷得像烧红的铁。我妹妹用一根棍子在上面画线。远处冰响了一声，我们一齐往后退。她问能不能从冰上走过去，我说不行。我们绕远路，沿着大道回了家。"},"imagine":{"tw":[["guess",0],["dream",3],["else",6],["suppose",0],["suspect",3],["maybe",6],["think",3]],"en":"I like to imagine a quiet town where nothing ever goes wrong. I suppose everyone has a dream like that. Maybe you think it is foolish. I guess I do, too. But when I suspect that something bad is coming, I go back to that picture and let it hold me. There is nothing else I can do about it. So I close my eyes and try to think of the light on the water. It is a small habit, but it has carried me through some hard mornings. My sister says I should live in the real world, and she is probably right.","zh":"我喜欢想象一座安静的镇子，那里从不出差错。我想每个人都有这样的梦吧。也许你觉得这很傻。我猜我也有点傻。可每当我猜到坏事要来时，我就回到那幅画面里，让它托着我。除此之外我也做不了什么。于是我闭上眼，努力去想水面上的光。这不过是个小习惯，却陪我熬过了一些难熬的清晨。我妹妹说我该活在现实里，她说的大概没错。"},"inside":{"tw":[["within",0],["belly",3],["surface",2],["empty",6],["interior",5],["midst",3],["hand",6]],"en":"Inside the old house everything was quiet. The interior was empty except for one chair, and the surface of the floor was grey with dust. A small bird had got within the walls and could not find its way out. I held it in the palm of my hand and felt its belly move. In the midst of that silence it seemed very loud. I carried it to the door and let it go. It sat on the step for a moment, as if deciding, and then flew straight up into the grey light.","zh":"老屋里面一片寂静。屋子里空荡荡的，只有一把椅子，地板表面蒙着灰色的尘。一只小鸟钻进了墙里，找不到出路。我把它捧在手心，感到它的肚子在动。在那片寂静当中，这动静显得很响。我把它拿到门口放走。它在台阶上停了一会儿，像在拿主意，然后直直飞进灰白的天光里。"},"key":{"tw":[["discover",0],["list",2],["major",6],["paint",0],["space",2],["step",6],["identify",0]],"en":"The key to the old shed was hidden under a stone. On the wall inside hung a list of names, and someone had used paint to mark a major date. I wanted to discover who had lived there, so I began to identify the families one by one. There was very little space on the page, and I had to write small. Step by step the whole story came together. I still have that list in a drawer, and sometimes I read the names aloud. Nobody in the family can remember them now.","zh":"旧棚子的钥匙藏在石头下面。里面墙上挂着一份名单，有人用油漆标出了一个重要的日子。我想弄清谁曾住在这里，便一个一个去辨认那些人家。纸上的空白很小，我只能写得很小。一步一步地，整个故事就拼了起来。那张单子还在我抽屉里，有时我会把名字念出声来。如今家里已没人记得他们了。"},"large":{"tw":[["big",0],["size",2],["small",1],["well",6],["great",5],["vast",6],["heavy",0]],"en":"A large table took up most of the room, far too big for the small kitchen. We measured its size twice, but it would not fit. My aunt said a great house needed great things, and this one was vast and heavy. It was well made, she added, and could not be cut down. In the end we left it where it stood and ate around it. For years it was the centre of that house. Every meal, every argument, every quiet evening happened at that table. When the house was sold, the new family kept it too, and I was glad.","zh":"一张大桌子占了屋里大半地方，对这间小厨房来说大得离谱。我们量了两遍尺寸，还是放不下。我姑妈说大房子就该配大东西，这张又大又沉。她还说做工很好，不能锯短。最后我们由它立在那儿，围着它吃饭。好多年里，它都是那所房子的中心。每一顿饭、每一次争吵、每一个安静的傍晚，都在这张桌边发生。房子卖掉后，新人家也把它留了下来，我很高兴。"},"luck":{"tw":[["chance",0],["misfortune",3],["condition",2],["good",6],["lot",0],["happy",6],["fortune",0]],"en":"Some people talk about luck as if it were a thing you could hold. My father said it was mostly chance and a good condition of mind. He had known his share of misfortune, and a lot of hard years, yet he stayed happy. He called it his fortune to have work and a warm room. I did not always believe him. But when things went well, I did not argue. He died in a bad winter, and I remember thinking that he had been right about most things. Not about luck, perhaps, but about the rest.","zh":"有些人谈运气，好像它是件能攥在手里的东西。我父亲说，那多半是机遇，加上一副好心态。他历过自己的那份不顺，也有过许多艰难的年份，可他一直高高兴兴。他把有活干、有间暖屋子叫做自己的福气。我并不总信他。可事情顺的时候，我也不争辩。他在一个寒冬里走了，我记得自己当时想，大多数事上他都是对的。也许不是运气，但是其余的一切。"}}});
